{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal","id":103062,"title":"Divis Mal, what's his deal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-31T19:08:49-07:00","id":103062,"title":"Divis Mal, what's his deal?","content":"Okay so could someone give me a thorough as Hell Run Down on the whole Divis Mal secret history thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T06:17:24-07:00","id":103333,"title":"","content":"Divas Mal, i believe, is considered one of the worlds 1st Novas. He was Doctor Primoris in the Adventure! setting. He believes that he and all Nova kind are above humanity and therefore above humanity's rules. which is why he wrote the Null Manifesto. What it boils down to is that he's an angry gay guy with a god complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T06:49:08-07:00","id":103352,"title":"","content":"Michael Donighal is presumably the first nova, yes, going back as far as the early 20th century. He was part of the original Aeon Society, which would in the Aberrant setting almost a century later found Project Utopia. He left Aeon sometime around World War 2 due to ideological differences: He wanted them to use their abilities to intervene in the world and steer the course of human history for the better. Maxwell Mercer, the founder of the Aeon Society and the guy he kinda had a crush on, had the opposite stance and believed they should limit themselves to inhibiting the influence of people like themselves so that humanity would be allowed to grow at its own pace.<br /> <br /> So when this became incredibly relevant, that is when World War 2 broke out, things went... poorly. We're not sure how much each side knew about the conflict (though with Maxwell Mercer being a time traveler, I'm personally convinced he knew about the Holocaust and chose to let it happen anyway because he thought it was a necessary event). After this little fight, Doctor Primoris (as he'd been calling himself at the time) disappears from history.<br /> <br /> He then reappears half a century later calling himself Divis Mal and, when novas first begin to erupt in large numbers he creates an ideological movement declaring that novas are a separate species from humanity and that they cannot be governed by human law. He has spent his isolation creating an entire transhumanist philosophy to go along with this.<br /> <br /> It ends badly, as it is one of the contributing factors to the Aberrant War. He disappears from history entirely after this event, and we never hear from him again. Some sources claim he eventually left our universe altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 04-01-2014, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T07:45:24-07:00","id":103386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=103352#post103352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Michael Donighal is presumably the first nova, yes, going back as far as the early 20th century. He was part of the original Aeon Society, which would in the Aberrant setting almost a century later found Project Utopia. He left Utopia sometime around World War 2 due to ideological differences: He wanted them to use their abilities to intervene in the world and steer the course of human history for the better. Maxwell Mercer, the founder of the Aeon Society and the guy he kinda had a crush on, had the opposite stance and believed they should limit themselves to inhibiting the influence of people like themselves so that humanity would be allowed to grow at its own pace.<br /> <br /> So when this became incredibly relevant, that is when World War 2 broke out, things went... poorly. We're not sure how much each side knew about the conflict (though with Maxwell Mercer being a time traveler, I'm personally convinced he knew about the Holocaust and chose to let it happen anyway because he thought it was a necessary event). After this little fight, Doctor Primoris (as he'd been calling himself at the time) disappears from history.<br /> <br /> He then reappears half a century later calling himself Divis Mal and, when novas first begin to erupt in large numbers he creates an ideological movement declaring that novas are a separate species from humanity and that they cannot be governed by human law. He has spent his isolation creating an entire transhumanist philosophy to go along with this.<br /> <br /> It ends badly, as it is one of the contributing factors to the Aberrant War. He disappears from history entirely after this event, and we never hear from him again. Some sources claim he eventually left our universe altogether.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that he was the one that caused the spike in eruptions due to the Galatia (SP) explosion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T17:12:22-07:00","id":103724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=103352#post103352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Michael Donighal is presumably the first nova, yes, going back as far as the early 20th century. He was part of the original Aeon Society, which would in the Aberrant setting almost a century later found Project Utopia. He left Aeon sometime around World War 2 due to ideological differences: He wanted them to use their abilities to intervene in the world and steer the course of human history for the better. Maxwell Mercer, the founder of the Aeon Society and the guy he kinda had a crush on, had the opposite stance and believed they should limit themselves to inhibiting the influence of people like themselves so that humanity would be allowed to grow at its own pace.<br /> <br /> So when this became incredibly relevant, that is when World War 2 broke out, things went... poorly. We're not sure how much each side knew about the conflict (though with Maxwell Mercer being a time traveler, I'm personally convinced he knew about the Holocaust and chose to let it happen anyway because he thought it was a necessary event). After this little fight, Doctor Primoris (as he'd been calling himself at the time) disappears from history.<br /> <br /> He then reappears half a century later calling himself Divis Mal and, when novas first begin to erupt in large numbers he creates an ideological movement declaring that novas are a separate species from humanity and that they cannot be governed by human law. He has spent his isolation creating an entire transhumanist philosophy to go along with this.<br /> <br /> It ends badly, as it is one of the contributing factors to the Aberrant War. He disappears from history entirely after this event, and we never hear from him again. Some sources claim he eventually left our universe altogether.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, right here. Michael Donighal is an extremely complex individual. In the early 1900s, Michael erupted as a nova due to the Hammersmith Incident, and was one of the founding members of the Aeon Society. The sheer magnitude of his Inspiration, both physical and in bearing, was incredible compared to his fellow Inspired -- he underwent a transformation so drastic that even friends by proxy (such as Whitley Styles, a charge of Maxwell Mercer) could hardly recognize him afterwards.<br /> <br /> Michael was certainly a close friend of Maxwell; and yes, it is strongly suggested that he held an unrequited love for Maxwell. He held Maxwell in high regard; in Michael's personal journals, he makes it clear that he and Maxwell have more than one strong ideological disagreements, and frequently encouraged (and ethically debated with) Maxwell in order to determine which of their ideologies was the most sound and appropriate. Regardless of these differences, though, Michael swore &quot;[He] would stand by [Maxwell], whichever path [Maxwell] choose[s]&quot;. For twenty years, he kept to his word; he offered a dissenting view for the Aeon Society, one of practicality and uncomfortable truths to play devil's advocate to their unrealistic and overly-optimistic ideas. It is worth noting, however, that Michael spent these twenty years constantly hoping that his friends were right, and they could prove him wrong.<br /> <br /> When imagining what the Aeon Society should be (or at least, what he BELIEVED it should be), Michael seemed conflicted. It is obvious that he wanted the Aeon Society to take a very public and forward role in guiding humanity's future -- he says as much quite clearly in a letter to Maxwell Mercer. However, his personal journals also express a sense of horror and guilt when discovering that &quot;so many men and women without [Michael's] advantages&quot; (such as being a nova) attempted to follow his example and 'save the world' in the manner of himself and his more capable associates -- his horror and guilt comes from the fact that the vast majority of those people died horribly in the attempt to emulate Michael's abilities. In laying out his suggested plans for the Aeon Society, Michael seems to imply that he wants to turn it into a &quot;city upon a hill&quot;, one that will guide humanity by example and direction; however, he seems to desire that an obvious distinction will be drawn between the Inspired individuals within the Aeon Society and the rest of humanity. He wants it be, &quot;Look at us, observe our capabilities, and let us lead you into tomorrow; but do not pretend to be like us, because you will hurt yourselves in the process. Let us take that burden for you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maxwell expresses a counter idea, suggesting that such action could be toxic for humanity in the long run. He believes that remaining behind the scenes is best; instead of telling humanity where to step, they should instead simply be there to pick them up when they stumble. His exact words are prophetic: &quot;You ask to stunt society's growth. The future will bring what the future brings. Humanity must remain free to develop in its own way. The times ahead will be hard, but humanity will recover. The near future may be grim, but the far future brings wonders neither of us have yet imagined. <b>If we seize history's reins, we will cripple humanity. What of human ambition when gods walk among men?</b>&quot; (Emphasis added)<br /> <br /> And Michael listens. He disagrees, but out of respect for his friend's ideals, he walks side-by-side with him. During the Second World War, those disagreements blossom and spiral out of control, resulting in some kind of fight between Michael and the rest of the Aeon Society. Details are intentionally vague, leaving it open to the Storytellers to individually decide what happens. Personally, I ran it such that witnessing Annabelle Lee Newfield's death (a young member of the Aeon Society who, like Michael did with Maxwell, held an unrequited love for Michael) was too much for him. His psyche, already strained from the humanitarian horrors of World War II, snapped, and he suffered a psychotic break. He attempted to forcibly take hold of the reigns of society to stop the bloodshed and violence, and in the process his means of doing so prompted the Aeon Society to intervene.<br /> <br /> Michael left, hid himself away, and gradually stitched his broken self back together. He assumed the named Divis Mal, and remained absent from world affairs for more than half a century. He was the one who began the Nova Age by initiating worldwide eruptions in 1998 (sources disagree on whether the Galatea explosion was a RESULT of his attempt, or the the INITIATING FACTOR of his attempt). After setting the spark of evolution, he sat back, and watched the world go by.<br /> <br /> And then Project Utopia got involved.<br /> <br /> Divis Mal's involvement in the creation of the Teragen is always a bit confusing, because we rarely hear <i>his</i> side of the story. Most often, it is told through the lens of N!'s talking heads, members of varying ideologies within the Teragen, and Project Utopia members. Is Divis Mal anti-baseline? Is he a nova supremacist? Does he believe that novas are inherently better than baselines, or that they are still human? Is he really suggesting that, because they are separate from baseline society, they are not bound by any of the legal or moral mores of that society?<br /> <br /> It's complicated, but think about it this way. View the entire thing -- from the 1920s to the 2000s -- from Michael Donighal's perspective. Maxwell Mercer is the man you love. You know he doesn't love you in return, but he does view you as one of his closest friends. This man is the man whom you respect more than any other person -- dead, alive, or yet to be born. When he vanished after the Hammersmith Incident, you refused to accept his death. You were willing to spend <i>your entire personal fortune</i> to engage in an almost <i>year-long quest across the entire planet</i> to find him, with no guarantee that he was still alive. You respect his views and vision to such an extent that, despite possibly being the most prideful individual on the planet, you set aside your personal qualms about his ideas and stood side-by-side with him till only your own emotional trauma tore you away from that man you love so much.<br /> <br /> And Project Utopia -- the child organization of the very group that your most respected loved one created -- shows up at the end of the 20th century. And their stated party line is the EXACT OPPOSITE of everything that the man you respected had stood for.<br /> <br /> Where Maxwell wanted subtlety, Project Utopia wants merchandizing.<br /> Where Maxwell wanted independence, Project Utopia wants everyone and everything to fall under their umbrella.<br /> Where Maxwell swore to never get involved where people did not want their involvement, Project Utopia forced themselves into every country and culture across the world.<br /> Where Maxwell understood the painful necessity of letting society make mistakes in order to learn from them, Project Utopia gleefully fixes any issue of baselines with nova abilities -- except they rarely correct the underlying cause, only the nasty effects of it, in order to create a shiny image that's good for the camera. Now, every society is being taught that &quot;it's ok to screw up, because the novas will just fix it&quot;.<br /> And, most offensive of all, Project Utopia dresses their novas in matching suits. They put their image everywhere. They teach the whole world that novas are the end-all, be-all of humanity. They begin taking control of society's direction, and refuse any attempts to let humanity make decisions of their own. Is it any wonder, then, that Maxwell's words to Michael might have rung clear once more in his mind? <b>&quot;If we seize history's reins, we will cripple humanity. What of human ambition when gods walk among men?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> With Maxwell nowhere to be found, the people he's left behind are utterly destroying EVERYTHING that you watched him sweat and toil and suffer and bleed to build. Your loved one, your respected teacher, your enlightened prophet of tomorrow, your embodiment of everything that humanity could hope to achieve, is slowly being destroyed under an unopposed march of easy-outs and someone-else's-problem solving.<br /> <br /> In response, a few years later, Michael proposes the philosophy that would become Teras. It is long, and it is eloquent, and it is embellished upon greatly by everyone who would hope to use it for their own ends. But what is at its core? What primary lesson does it try to get across?<br /> <br /> &quot;We are no longer human, and we must no longer participate in human society. Instead, we must now chart our own path.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is it any surprise, then, that Michael suggests this philosophy in response to Project Utopia's statements? At this point, it's mostly conjecture, and I can't say this with the authority of &quot;I'm quoting directly from the books&quot;, but I believe -- I FIRMLY believe -- that Michael is not doing this with the impetus of nova supremacy. He's personally witnessed the horrors of the Holocaust, you don't just <i>forget </i>that. Rather, I believe that he is trying his best to continue his loved one's legacy, using what he has and the position he holds. I believe that Michael created the Teragen with the intent (misguided, perhaps, with the benefit of hindsight) to encourage novas to separate themselves from baseline society -- NOT as a result of ideas of supremacy, but instead to give humanity the chance to progress on their own. To make their own mistakes, and not rely on novas to fix them and clean up. To make their own choices, and not be swayed (intentionally or otherwise) by the novas around them. To be able to happily pursue their own desires and lives and hopes and aspirations, without the oppressively omnipresent realization that no matter what they do, a nova can do it better.<br /> <br /> After all, what would happen to human ambition when gods walk among men?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2464,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","user":"lustral_star","date":".  Fixed an error Ian pointed out. 06-28-2014, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T17:57:06-07:00","id":103735,"title":"","content":"Hmmm one mystery to is what Exactly is Divis Mal's powers? What was his power evolution? Why do people assume he left the universe? Is he present in Aeon? I remember it being theorized by some people that he became Malfeas in Exalted. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:03:31-07:00","id":103737,"title":"","content":"Now, that is an impressive analysis of Divis Mal. It really makes the character seem more real to me, but it also seems to me that it conflicts strongly with my understanding of the things Divis Mal did, Atrocities associated with him performed by his own hand. But then again, I'm far from anything resembling an expert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:06:33-07:00","id":103741,"title":"","content":"Michael's powers are left vague -- they're essentially, &quot;whatever the Storyteller needs him to have&quot;. In the 1920s, it was known that he possessed the ability to sense Telluric Energy; he could also track people down over large distances. He demonstrated supernatural grace, intelligence, and beauty. Many of his abilities appeared to cross the boundaries of mesmerists and stalwarts -- it seemed as though he could do it all.<br /> <br /> By the Nova Age, there are a few things that are either known or inferred:<ul><li>He has a Quantum rating of 8</li> <li>He has every Mega Attribute at a minimum of 3, and several at 5 (or more)</li> <li>He has enough Mega-enhancements to accomplish just about whatever he needs to, given time and effort</li> <li>He has:<ul><li>Armor</li> <li>Disrupt</li> <li>Immolate (plasma)</li> <li>Quantum Bolt (plasma)</li> <li>Elemental Anima (plasma)</li> <li>Elemental Mastery (plasma)</li> <li>Flight</li> <li>Hypermovement</li> <li>Disintegration</li> <li>etc, etc.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> The exact list, and really the only indication of his capabilities, is located on page 154 of the book Aberrant Worldwide, Phase I. It's strongly suggested that he has a way of hijacking global communications/radio waves, and he either constructed a device to initiate a surge of Quantum energy across the world or possess an innate ability (read: power) to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:16:40-07:00","id":103748,"title":"","content":"Interesting so he had power set was very much like a Sun God or some such. Would it be fair to say his main powers were either enhanced intelligence or charisma?<br /> <br /> And I take it he didn't age? Is that common with Novas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:17:30-07:00","id":103750,"title":"","content":"To answer your other questions on why it's assumed he left the universe, the vast majority of that is fan speculation. I believe according to the unpublished (yet available online) Trinity Storyteller's Handbook, it makes a sidelong mention that Divis Mal left the universe when he realized how much his presence and actions had hurt people, and how badly he had f----d up. If he were doing this, mechanically, he could be doing one of two things.<ul><li>He's using a level 4 power, Crosstime Travel, in order to leave to an alternate timeline or a universe with very different physical laws</li> </ul><br /> Or<ul><li>He's using a level 6 power, Create Universe, which does exactly what it says on the tin. Using this power, the new universe one creates may have any physical laws or concepts of reality that one may conceive. A nova's new universe is in no way constrained by the physical laws of the nova's originating universe.</li> </ul><br /> As far as I know, there is no <i>official</i> mention that Michael/Divis Mal is associated with other White Wolf game lines and universes. What probably happened was that someone mentioned on a thread, saying &quot;Hey, wouldn't it be [awesome/hilarious/cool] if Divis Mal used Create Universe to make [Exalted's Creation/The Old World of Darkness/The New World of Darkness/a universe filled with chocolate/a place where he was the only one who had arms/etc.]?&quot;<br /> <br /> This probably caught people's fancy, and it was repeated frequently enough as a fun fan theory that it is often &quot;accepted&quot; by fans as what happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:22:28-07:00","id":103753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=103748#post103748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting so he had power set was very much like a Sun God or some such. Would it be fair to say his main powers were either enhanced intelligence or charisma?<br /> <br /> And I take it he didn't age? Is that common with Novas?</div> </div> </div> </div>His powers were less like a Sun God <i>in a thematic or philosophical sense</i>, and more like a literal star <i>in a physical embodiment sense</i>. Michael (as his namesake suggests) demonstrated many fire-related abilities, and his &quot;quantum template&quot; seemed focused on plasma and fire. He did not, however, enjoy the position of leading with ideology like a god; instead, he preferred rationalism and logic. And yes, he did not seem to age noticeably. Even the weakest nova has a life expectancy of 150 years; increasing levels of Mega Stamina can raise that to several thousand, and there is more than one Mega Enhancement which literally enables you to stop aging and live (barring accident or injury) forever.<br /> <br /> His main powers were, perhaps, not his charisma -- though he is most well-known for his intelligence. Even before he erupted, Michael was brilliant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:40:39-07:00","id":103760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=103737#post103737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, that is an impressive analysis of Divis Mal. It really makes the character seem more real to me, but it also seems to me that it conflicts strongly with my understanding of the things Divis Mal did, Atrocities associated with him performed by his own hand. But then again, I'm far from anything resembling an expert.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another interesting foible. Yes, Divis Mal did things -- <i>terrible things </i>-- toward the end of the Nova Age. Startlingly, they conflict drastically with his own thoughts and ideas for the entire century prior. What the hell happened? What made him change so much, in such little time?<br /> <br /> I've been running an Adventure!/Aberrant/Trinity game for almost two years, and a big part of it is that the characters were around at the very beginning. They've been with these NPCs since the very start, and they've seen Michael rise and fall. So, I had to come up with a reason for why such a noble person would wind up doing what he did. He not only <i>allowed</i> extreme elements within the Teragen to outright murder the more moderate and philosophical elements, he <i>personally authorized</i> the murder of Jeremiah Scripture, his lover and confidant <i>for the past 50 years</i>. How could his mind have changed so much?<br /> <br /> We arrived at two conclusions. It's suggested that Divis Mal had his ethical about-face soon after leaving one of his (many) trips through Chrysalis.<br /> <br /> The easiest explanation we came up with is that he botched his Chrysalis; something happened while he was in that comatose state, and his mind was left warped -- an inversion of what he believed he stood for. When he left Chrysalis, he was cruel, vindictive, and uncaringly ready for blood.<br /> <br /> However, I felt that this was far too simplistic: why would the man who <i>invented</i> the process of Chrysalis have screwed it up so badly? I also felt that it took the responsibility of what happened to the world and pinned it on the chance of dice, a random event that has no emotion. It didn't <i>tell a story</i>.<br /> <br /> So, I suggested an alternate theory: There is a man within the Teragen known as The Apostle. Long story short, he's an a--hole. He's a brown noser, a quantum-powered sycophant, and he's <i>obsessed</i> with Divis Mal. While Scripture views Divis Mal as a man (albeit a highly enlightened one), Apostle views Divis Mal <i>as a literal god</i>. The Apostle is also shown to be completely happy with straight-up betraying people; he's got a real Judas Complex. He betrays his own teacher, Caroline Fong, to Project Utopia when she's in Chrysalis. He mentally manipulates (using his quantum powers or just threatening) anyone to get his way, and if they won't budge, he just has them eliminated. It is stated in the description of Chrysalis, that it provides the nova with a fair amount of physical protection against attacks. However, it provides <i>no protection for their mind</i>. It also states that they are essentially comatose -- even if they have any awareness of the outside world at all, they're powerless to do anything about it. I proposed the theory that Apostle, tired of Scripture &quot;having Divis Mal all to himself&quot;, and tired of Divis Mal not taking the hardline stance that Apostle constantly espouses, managed to find some way to manipulate Divis Mal while he was in Chrysalis. It wouldn't be <i>impossible</i>; do it slowly enough, over the years he was out, and telepathically change a memory here or an emotion there... by the time he was done, Divis Mal would have emerged from Chrysalis a complete changed man. He began to embody the ideas that he had <i>earlier</i> explicitly expressed hating, yet Apostle had mentioned them as being what Divis Mal needed to do. He coldly authorized Scripture's death, and the Apostle suddenly and strangely became his right-hand man.<br /> <br /> I should point out that, while the individual elements were all there, this was a personal theory of my group, and is not by any means official. It places the events of the Aberrant War more closely on human (and nova) pride. It shows that Michael <i>thought</i> he was good enough, but his own pride on his incorruptibility led to his own downfall. It showcases something that I want my Aberrant game to express: No matter how much you want to, no matter how much you try, you <i>can't change human nature</i>. Only other people can change themselves. Michael thought he could, but he paid the price, and the people around him paid the price as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T19:00:08-07:00","id":103768,"title":"","content":"The big source on the 'universe creation' thing was, for me at least, the Trinity Storytellers Handbook outline that was posted after the Trinity Universe lines were discontinued. <a href=\"http://rpgbooks.wikia.com/wiki/Trinity_Storytellers_Handbook\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpgbooks.wikia.com/wiki/Trini...llers_Handbook</a> the whole thing can be found here.<br /> <br /> The specific sidebar I'm referring to can be found in this section: <a href=\"http://rpgbooks.wikia.com/wiki/Trinity_Storytellers_Handbook/Chapter_Three:_Aberrant_Society#Future_Fates\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpgbooks.wikia.com/wiki/Trini...y#Future_Fates</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T19:13:39-07:00","id":103778,"title":"","content":"Ah! There it is!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T23:47:36-07:00","id":103875,"title":"","content":"Of course, we're probably never going to get official commentary on this stuff from the writers. So, fan theories AWAAAY!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T05:17:56-07:00","id":103973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=103724#post103724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he was not a nova at the time, then he was certainly the most powerful Stalwart in the world</div> </div> </div> </div>Novas and stalwarts are the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T07:26:42-07:00","id":104026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=103973#post103973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Novas and stalwarts are the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, good point! Thank you for catching that. Officially, novas and stalwarts are identical. I did run them as being different stops on the same evolutionary path, but that was fannon and unofficial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T07:32:47-07:00","id":104033,"title":"","content":"Well, our discussions managed to catch IAN'S attention, of all people, if only to correct a glaring taxological mistake I made. I'm feeling far more fanboy glee than I've any right to. Anyone else have ideas on Michael that they've encountered in their stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T08:16:48-07:00","id":104059,"title":"","content":"There is one detail from the Teragen Splatbook that's usually overlooked: The Teragen in its infancy was not actaully a creation of Divis mal, he came along a few years after it's formation as a roundtable discussion group formed by Mathematician, Orzaiz, and later Fong and Apostle. It was implied that he had been watching for such a group to form on its own and then had Scripture (who has contact with Mathematician) subtly feed the discussion group various bits of Mal's philosophy. Once they came around naturally to somethgn approximating his way of thinking he joined them and largely usurped all authority, but he largely let them do as they wished (which they complain endlessly about).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T11:24:52-07:00","id":104190,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Michael may have provided them with a philosophy around which to base themselves, but the inner group was already present and talking amongst themselves by the time he showed up. Caroline, I believe, was the one who took Michael's philosophy and ideas of Chrysalis, and expanded upon them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T07:11:48-07:00","id":104796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=104033#post104033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, our discussions managed to catch IAN'S attention, of all people, if only to correct a glaring taxological mistake I made. I'm feeling far more fanboy glee than I've any right to. Anyone else have ideas on Michael that they've encountered in their stories?</div> </div> </div> </div>I at the very least scan over every post made in this forum. Why wouldn't I?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T08:39:34-07:00","id":104850,"title":"","content":"Because you're awesome like that, Ian, and we're all very happy you've an interest and investment in this project. I mean, realistically speaking, you could just ignore the chattering fans, but you and the other devs don't. Which is fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T10:42:45-07:00","id":104936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=104850#post104850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because you're awesome like that, Ian, and we're all very happy you've an interest and investment in this project. I mean, realistically speaking, you could just ignore the chattering fans, but you and the other devs don't. Which is fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Ian was the main man behind that trinity Storytellers guide that never got released so he's been in the thick of this setting for a long while. I don't think the Continuum could be in better hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T22:09:00-07:00","id":109836,"title":"","content":"That was a wonderful read. I loved going through that thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T09:48:13-07:00","id":129939,"title":"","content":"I'm running my own campaign that deals with what happens to Pax and what happens to Mal to make him declare war on humanity. Basically after Pax was defeated by Mal during Phase I It did a real number on his Ego and started his downward spiral into insanity. He became obsessed with finding a way to destroy Mal, no matter what it took, and taking his place as number one badass Nova on the planet. As it so happens Mal's introduction to the world and his defeat of Pax terrified the world's governments into drastic. As a result Utopia, along with the Directive and Proteus stepped up its research into Quantum powers. Eventually they're able to create a device based off the old Hammersmith device that feeds Quantum energy directly into a Nova's body drastically increasing their power, but building massive amounts of Taint. Pax volunteers to be the first test subject for the device in order to gain enough power to defeat Mal. Needless to say the device makes Pax more powerful but it completely destroys any sanity he has left. Itching for a rematch with Mal he violently attacks any Terat he can find (Geryon, Raoul, The Confederate and Shrapnel are killed during his rampage) in an effort to bring Mal out of hiding. It eventually works and Pax gets the rematch he wants. With his new powers Pax is pretty evenly matched with Mal and is able to injure him during the beginning of the fight. Both Nova's tap deeply into their quantum powers and cause severe collateral damage during their fight, killing millions of people during the process. Mal is eventually able to use his greater understanding of Quantum to gain the upper hand but he is forced to have to kill Pax, something that shocks Mal to his core.The battle between Pax and Mal horrifies baseline human's around the world and turns public opinion against Nova's. Due to the severe damage to his body and his lingering anger he feels toward Utopia and their forcing his hand to kill another Nova, Mal starts to become more violent and megalomanical in his stance against baseline humans which will eventually explode into full blown war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2904-stonepedal1","name":"stonepedal1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T11:46:26-07:00","id":130042,"title":"","content":"Of course, one if his more prominent features that often gets overlooked in polite society is the fact that he has arms. He just flaunts them around, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","name":"Ravenmancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:59:17-07:00","id":132949,"title":"","content":"His arms are just flappin' all over the place, like a certain green frog. Control yourself, Michael! Keep your arms to yourself!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2464,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","user":"lustral_star","date":". 05-11-2014, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:27:22-07:00","id":142897,"title":"","content":"lustral_star, good postings <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I myself find Divis Mal to be a worthless NPC. It's like they made a game where the players live in a world that tell Divis Mal's story. The player characters are just there to witness his awesomeness.<br /> <br /> It is nice to see someone explain why they think that character might have some worth, though. I am just starting up a campaign and have no idea what I will do with Divis Mal. My players (both old and new Aberrant players) find him silly and somewhat embarrassing, and I can't help but to agree.<br /> <br /> I view him as insane. None with mega charisma and mega manipulation would make that manifesto if they didn't want a conflict with humanity. With Megas it should in fact be possible to word it in such a way that people would cheer him on. Also, if he has mega intelligence he simply must have a feeling about where his journey will take both him and humanity, but the war and a space armada still obviously came as a surprise to him. He is just a big pile of epic fail.<br /> <br /> The only way I see to make the players take the character serious is to make him utterly insane (or remove mega charisma, mega manipulation and mega intelligence). He might look like he is alright, he may say the right thing, but you should see in his eyes that he isn't really home any more. There is also the option to just kill him off and introduce a character that is more believable. ATM I am leaning toward insanity and introducing another force that can represent the potential of novas.<br /> <br /> My players had a fun idea though, that Divis Mal is just a figurehead for others in Teragen, that he is a dim-witted fool with a lot of quantum muscles and no brain. A perfect tool to make people believe that you have some kind of master plan. I find the idea somewhat seductive. It would explain a lot IMO, and it would be fun.<br /> <br /> Either way, I appreciate the postings in this thread. I find it valuable to read some well thought through ideas and opinions about Divis Mal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3066-samiloth","name":"Samiloth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T09:24:21-07:00","id":143559,"title":"","content":"Lustral, that's a really nice analysis of Divis Mal. Some of it is conjecture, but it's pretty well reasoned and I have to say that it mirrors a lot of what I thought about him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T20:30:57-07:00","id":144050,"title":"","content":"Thank you, all. I tried my best to delineate the boundaries between what's cannon from the books (pretty much everything up to WWII) and what's my own hypothesis and the answers to ambiguous questions I had to answer for my game (the specifics of Annabelle's death, the exact manner in which Michael fought with the Aeon Society, and his &quot;true&quot; intentions behind the Null Manifesto). The journal entries and personal letters in Adventure! are a treasure trove of information for Michael, and a wonderful read in general.<br /> <br /> One thing I try to explore in my Aberrant games (and something which informed and modeled my choices for portraying Michael) is that novas (Michael included) are still human. They're not literal gods or &quot;perfect&quot; beings, they're just humans with preternatural (and frequently supernatural) capabilities. However, they still have <i>some</i> limitations, no matter what. Being Mega-Intelligent does not mean you know everything, it just means you know more than any normal human. Likewise, while Michael is supposed to be <i>brilliant</i>, he is not omniscient. He still makes mistakes on occasion, as evidenced by the Aberrant War. Of course, we really can't pin that whole thing on him, that's ****** trite and cliche. There were more factors involved than just himself and his decisions -- there was also an entire planet filled with 7 billion other people, humans and novas alike, some of whom were probably even more intelligent than Michael. Mistakes were made by billions of people over a course of 60 years -- three human generations! -- and the world paid a dear price for those mistakes. The conjectures I made were heavily influenced by my decisions to <i>not</i> put the spotlight on Michael, and let everyone else's choices mean something.<br /> <br /> Maybe he saw it all coming at some point, and chose not to intervene because &quot;this is their choice&quot;. Maybe he saw it all coming, but thought it could be stopped. Maybe he just didn't trust his predictions, and mistakenly put his hope in a sense of human optimism. I think a big thing to keep in mind for Aberrant, whether dealing with Michael or not, is that we can frequently fall prey to the same thoughts that baseline humanity did in the Aberrant age: since someone is smarter/wittier/better than <i>what we are</i>, that must mean they know everything or have all the answers. While novas deserve a lot of credit, we sometimes give them <i>far more</i> credit than what they actually deserve. They might become more than human in several ways, but in many others they almost always remain painfully mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T05:22:28-07:00","id":144372,"title":"","content":"I've always felt this was the cool thing about Aberrant... Aberrant was about what happened when you gave superpowers to random people and not paragons of Good or masters of Villiany as it usually is in the comic books. The way how most Novas just went around capitalising their skills and the world turned them into starlets of the highest order was a very reasonable way of going into it.<br /> <br /> The fact that the one who claims to be more then human is the one who is most human in his foibles was a really nice way of emphasising the human element of Aberrant. In Trinity, this element was clearly no longer necessary, and the Aberrants were removed from their humanity to become more compelling villians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T05:43:03-07:00","id":144402,"title":"","content":"And then we get the funky Taint babies made of screaming mercury, and Aberrants lead into Lovecraftian terror from beyond the stars. Or, at least, otherwise incomprehensible foes due to their inhumanity at the time. Nice bit of horror to the Space Opera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:33:34-07:00","id":182577,"title":"","content":"It took three months for me to fix that error Ian pointed out. Wow, lazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:43:20-07:00","id":182586,"title":"","content":"In my own slightly altered house-version of the continuity, &quot;Doctor Primoris&quot; was a Stalwart, not a Nova, though over the decades he did rise to be the most powerful Stalwart while in other cases the phenomena of the Inspiration Age was fading away. He doesn't make is first appearance as a Nova till after he and Mercer had their fateful confrontation in 1945 afterwhich they both disappeared.<br /> <br /> My touch on canon here? The exact date of this confrontation in July 16th - at a place called <i><b>Trinity</b></i>.<br /> <br /> I think you can imagine the circumstances of that date that would result in both disappearing in a flash of blinding light...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:45:32-07:00","id":182587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=103973#post103973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Novas and stalwarts are the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, fair enough, but at least as Adventure! and Aberrant present them there is a definite difference in power-level going on!<br /> <br /> My point is he graduates from the Adventure! powerlevel Stalwart to the Aberrant powerlevel Nova on July 16, 1945, in Trinity New Mexico at the culmination of his battle with Mercer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T22:02:01-07:00","id":182609,"title":"","content":"That's an interesting take. And yeah, the way it was originally presented, it made it seem as though Stalwarts were &quot;Nova-lite&quot; and Mesmerists were &quot;Psiad-lite&quot;. I have since learned that's not quite what they were intending, and it was supposed to be &quot;They are the same thing, just with different levels of power&quot;. Hence, the change.<br /> <br /> Since I had my PCs take part in the fight against Michael, I couldn't leave it to just Mercer and Michael. I actually involved the entire Aeon Society (sans Annabelle, because she... well. You know.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T08:19:43-07:00","id":182907,"title":"","content":"Wait a minute. I was an avid afferent player while the game line was out. I have all of the printed materials and any and all PDF format materials that never made it to print, I think.from where is this information about Mal authorizing scriptures death and the apostle becoming his right hand man? I do Aemember reading that this was the Apostles ambition, but in what source material is actually come to pass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3389-druid","name":"Druid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3389_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T08:42:26-07:00","id":182930,"title":"","content":"And by the way, I'm positive I read a mansion or two of the appearance of a completely tainted out Divas Mal in the Trinity timeline. am I completely delusional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3389-druid","name":"Druid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3389_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:26:14-07:00","id":183043,"title":"","content":"In the Teragen book, while discussing &quot;The Night of Long Knives.&quot; And on the note of Trinity, Divis Mal is MENTIONED, like a boogeyman, but never actually appears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:28:22-07:00","id":183044,"title":"","content":"As far as <b>Trinity</b> is concerned, Divis Mal is gone and not coming back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:32:06-07:00","id":183045,"title":"","content":"Poor Michael.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T23:55:32-07:00","id":184623,"title":"","content":"Every time I read an issue of &quot;The Boys&quot;, I thought of Aberrant. This thread makes me sad I never took the time to really read Adventure! back in the day.<br /> <br /> I always took Mal and Pax as being reflected allegories. Pax becomes the ultimate expression of stagnation and the Status Quo, while Mal becomes the personification of evolution and free will. Mal fancied himself Natural Selection personified. He instigated these horrors as a means of driving human evolution forwards through conflict, wheras Pax sought to inhibit any kind of non-approved societal change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T07:03:40-07:00","id":187028,"title":"","content":"Do you mean Max, instead of Pax?<br /> <br /> Cause Pax would be Caestus Pax, the showboating celebrity superman-wannabe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T12:12:04-07:00","id":187299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=187028#post187028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean Max, instead of Pax?<br /> <br /> Cause Pax would be Caestus Pax, the showboating celebrity superman-wannabe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairly certain he means Pax since Pax is basically the face of Team Tomorrow and the Utopia Project. While the Utopia Project has utopian ideals (sort of), much of what it does in the undertones and in the non-Utopia books is restrict and prevent change. On the one hand that's a good thing because a lot of radical changes can lead to the rapid destabilization and collapse of society. On the other hand they very much act like an oppressive big brother figure which is intent on ensuring that they're seen as the font of all wisdom and goodness. Pax, as the head of Team Tomorrow, was basically building himself up as the World's Cop and cops are very much about inhibiting non-approved societal change (that is functionally what laws are about).<br /> <br /> Another way to think of the reflection is that Mal is very much about personal responsibility and freedoms where as Pax, being the proverbial lapdog of Utopia, is very much about following orders from on high, which is arguably the opposite of freedom will (especially given Proteus and Utopia's hidden agendas).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1940,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1940-whitejoker","user":"WhiteJoker","date":". 07-03-2014, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1940-whitejoker","name":"WhiteJoker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T14:56:36-07:00","id":187434,"title":"","content":"yeah.. was just going by Aberrant.. I'm not overly familiar with Adventure! yet..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T08:31:18-07:00","id":188002,"title":"","content":"by the way, is there any image of Divis Mal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T10:43:13-07:00","id":188064,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://bork63.tripod.com/Divis.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Here he is on the left of the Aberrant cover</a>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wiki.rpg.net/images/c/ca/MPost13355-Aeon.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">That's the young pre-Mal Donighal in the sunglasses in Adventure!</a><br /> <br /> The picture of him setting fire to the UN Secretary General's skeleton and smiling from <b>Trinity</b> doesn't seem to be online. I think it's fairly important to understanding him as well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T13:31:43-07:00","id":188209,"title":"","content":"Craig's first link won't work since Tripod doesn't allow hotlinking. Here it is rehosted: <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/CQqJeKr.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i.imgur.com/CQqJeKr.jpg</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T14:10:05-07:00","id":188228,"title":"","content":"I always liked the picture of Mal in jeans and a t-shirt hanging out in a club. Made him seem a bit more human than the face he liked to wear for people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T16:38:09-07:00","id":188298,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it is just me but I got the feeling Divis Mal, as a bogeyman in Trinity, was not getting a fair<br /> shake. As far as I really read all he did was, issue the Null Manifesto, Not stop the &quot;Night of long Knives&quot;, and incinerate the Secretary General of the UN<br /> The Teregen Sourcebook says that as you get more powerful as a Terat you don't go insane but you become more inhuman. What if Adventure Dr. Promtius was trying to do the right thing. Early Abberant Divis Mal just wanted people to grow to his level so Current Time Abberant Divis Mal Let the Teragen become what it wanted to be become because he felt leading it even in a &quot;Humain&quot; direction would be counter-productive. Divis Mal didn't thing he should stop the &quot;Night of Long Knives&quot; but there is nothing to say he could have stopped it. Finally given that China had launched a nuclear strike and issued an ultimatum, killing one person might have been a very restrained reaction.<br /> <br /> Personally I would run him as going from human in Adventure to hard to get a handle on in Aberrant to Not present and impossible to comprehend in Trinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3424-patrick-chapman","name":"Patrick Chapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T11:18:20-08:00","id":333234,"title":"","content":"Nothing to add here but another round of congratulations for Lustral_star's exposition. Great stuff, i wish i could have posed it so eloquently to my brother who takes the &quot;Mal is a hate-monger&quot; approach. The apostle inference is a very clever solution to the strange gap between the two depictions..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  needed moar praise. 12-07-2014, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T14:16:20-08:00","id":365742,"title":"","content":"Moar praise!<br /> <br /> Wow, still getting responses over this. I'm pretty flattered. I think a good chunk of the reason behind all of what I wrote is due to the fact that my game is covering the entire Aeonverse timeline, and the party was so close to Michael in a personal sense. It really forced me to look at him as a person, instead of a distant caricature that only shows up in passing to move plot along. Since the party has been keeping up with him from the beginning, they're in the same general power-level as Michael, which means they frequently meet him as a peer instead of a god. Really made me pay attention to him and read between the lines; I was pleasantly shocked when I did, as suddenly everything began making SO MUCH SENSE. Especially reading through his personal notes and journal entries in Adventure!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T05:30:37-08:00","id":366206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=365742#post365742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moar praise!<br /> <br /> Wow, still getting responses over this. I'm pretty flattered.</div> </div> </div> </div>You clearly put some thought into that analysis - you deserve the recognition, many of us have been mulling it over for years in the back of our heads. If this is how you treated Micheal, i'd rather love to see how you've managed the other mysteries the setting leaves unanswered between Adventure! and Aberrant. Is there anywhere i can do so, a synopsis or something? It might not really fit with the Divis-Mal specific topic at hand to enquire here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=365742#post365742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really made me pay attention to him and read between the lines; I was pleasantly shocked when I did, as suddenly everything began making SO MUCH SENSE. Especially reading through his personal notes and journal entries in Adventure!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found a lot of joy and eureka between the lines of the the aeon settings, I'm glad to see it isn't all false pattern recognition. Gladder still to see a detailed framework for what lurked between the lines 'by' Micheal during the early years - and then spread so thinly over many other (seeminlgy contradictory) books. I never thought to look so hard at Apostle in the Teragen - i had some of the rest worked out, but not as well.<br /> Just in relation to the character's arc in your campaign, how did you resolve the tension between Micheal and Max to put it to sleep? Considering the level of build the books put toward this conflict - it seems anti-climax is inevitable, due to all the propaganda surrounding both sides by the nova-age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Apostle is not Scripture and vice versa 01-11-2015, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T16:29:24-08:00","id":366711,"title":"","content":"Don't forget he has arms too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T20:35:13-08:00","id":366916,"title":"","content":"Nihilist, I'll do what I can tomorrow. Got a day of teaching chemistry and then discussion with IRB, so it's packed, but I can put together some things about what I've done in my continuity, and where I'm going with it, whenever I can make the time.<br /> <br /> ARMS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2464,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","user":"lustral_star","date":".  moar arms 01-11-2015, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T09:49:02-08:00","id":371145,"title":"","content":"I've given a lot of thought to what Michael was like pre-Hammersmith, but it remains to be seen how much that'll end up in Trinity. Most of my focus has been getting the system ready (dramatic editing is coming next week).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T18:45:19-08:00","id":371683,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a house-rule for some games that includes a -1 Inspiration cost bump (or +1 die bonus) if the player shouts, &quot;BUT SUDDENLY--!&quot; when describing the dramatic edit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T09:53:00-08:00","id":372662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=371683#post371683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a house-rule for some games that includes a -1 Inspiration cost bump (or +1 die bonus) if the player shouts, &quot;BUT SUDDENLY--!&quot; when describing the dramatic edit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'm currently modeling them on updated Anticipation/Declaration rules following some slightly updated principles. It does require Inspiration, though there's a &quot;Lucky&quot; Edge that gives you a phantom bump if you're not Inspired. For a Talent, DE ain't something you do consciously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T10:18:44-08:00","id":372690,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty good. When describing DE to someone who had never played Adventure! before, I typically encapsulated it as:<br /> <br /> Imagine a pulpy Doc Savage comic, or radio drama. The heroes are in a bind, it looks like tragedy is about to strike, and then the Narrator shouts, &quot;But suddenly...!&quot; The 'but suddenly' is a player triggering a DE, and everything that follows it is the DE itself.<br /> <br /> That usually gets an, &quot;Oh, I get it!&quot; response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:23:30-07:00","id":453084,"title":"","content":"Wow, I can't believe I'm posting to an Aeonverse thread after all these years...<br /> <br /> Divis Mal is not Magneto. I preface my commentary this way because I'm about to compare the two while noting lots of similarities, but to be clear: I am fully aware that Divis Mal is his own character, with a unique character arc, that is not the same as Erik Magnus Lensherr's (or if you prefer, Max Eisenhardt's). Now, having said that:<br /> <br /> Michael Donigal is the best friend of the man who founded an organization (in a private mansion at first, no less), dedicated to teaching the nascent Inspired to use their gifts for the betterment of a mankind that would inevitably come to fear them. This man is an idealist, one might even say utopian, with incredible abilities of his own, whose small group of friends would eventually become a sprawling alliance that strives to use its powers for a better world -- sometimes at odds with its idealistic founder. Michael, meanwhile, has a fundamental, somewhat violent break with his dear friend, and co-founds an organization of evolved supermen who stand in philosophical opposition to this organization. Widely derided as evil, this organization nevertheless has members who simply believe in founding their own separate society, while others range from defenders of their own to psychotics every bit as monstrous as the propaganda says. Meanwhile, Michael himself is a brilliant, charismatic winner of the Superpower Lottery who wields a god-like energy suite with unparalleled power and precision. Sound familiar?<br /> <br /> While Michael is not Magnus, the two have a lot of clear overlap, especially in Magneto's sane periods, and the Claremont Magneto (upon whom the 90s X-Men cartoon version is very strongly based) heavily informs my portrayal of him. Donigal once believed -- or at least, desperately wanted to believe -- in Max Mercer's vision. His deep personal traumas and the horrors of World War II eventually made this impossible. Primoris/Mal desperately tries to avoid open conflict with Max's stepchildren during the Nova Age, but Mal sees that time as <i>his,</i> and when the world goes to war with his people, he fights back. <i>If</i> he really murdered that unfortunate human on his way out -- and we should be suspicious of all pre-crash records in Trinity, IMO -- it was an atypical event, as a warning or a last bitter shot, but not indicative of his nature. (Unless you want to go with the Apostle theory, which is <i>awesome,</i> IMO.) The takeaway for me is, the Nova Age Mal is solely concerned with &quot;his&quot; people, and thinks it's best for humans and novas to chart separate paths. I'm not sure how he feels about psiads by then, but extrapolation implies that he would think it best for them to go their own way, separate from baselines and novas alike. For an excellent portrayal of Magneto who charts closely to the Aeon Society Donigal, watch X-Men: First Class, quite possibly the best version of the Xavier-Magnus friendship to date.<br /> <br /> Note: none of this is intended to step on lustral_star's phenomenal analysis of the character, but as a far too old fan of both X-Men and the Aeonverse, I had to note the conceptual ancestry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T01:32:38-07:00","id":462023,"title":"","content":"Part of Divis Mal's deal is that he's been through the Chrysalis multiple times - which results in cumulative penalties to understand or socialize with mundane humans. Assuming the count in the <i>Teragen</i> book is accurate, and he entered chrysalis at the minimum levels each time, he's got <i>at least</i> a +3 penalty (i.e. base difficulty of 10) to any social roll involving baselines. As others have pointed out, he just doesn't think like mundane humans any more, and that limits his ability to anticipate their reactions, or have normal, healthy relationships with them (and that's before including any possible mental aberrations he may suffer). Heck, the <i>Teragen</i> book implies that he's having problems maintaining normal relationships with other novas!<br /> <br /> Another big aspect of his personality (and subsequent dealings with the world) is that Divis Mal seems to have been deeply influenced by Nietzsche. If you've never read Nietzsche, his work basically postulates that modern standards of good and evil have been corrupted and subverted by the elites/one percenters/powers-that-be into concepts that merely uphold the status quo, and keeping themselves in power. But Nietzsche also postulated that the time was right for a &quot;superhuman&quot; (ubermensch), someone who would defy such labels, overthrow the status quo, and open a new dawn of possibilities to the world. Sound familiar?<br /> <br /> And in the Aeon Society, Mal probably sees those beliefs (about the corruption of &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot;) firmly validated. Sure, Aeon is backing Project Utopia . . . .but they're also firmly supporting Project Proteus. And Proteus . . . wow, they're into some seriously evil things. Assassinations and black sites. Kidnapping and torture. Raping female novas, so that Project Proteus scientists can dissect the kids to see what second generation novas will be like. During the time of <i>Aberrant</i>, Aeon is effectively the Red Cross - just with death camps.<br /> <br /> And no one seems to care. When Corbin finally gets hard proof about Proteus, the UN turns him over . . . .to the Aeon Society. Later, during the Aberrant War, Aeon endorses the genocide of anyone related to novas (even former Project Utopia members), and destroys all nova-based research it can find, plunging civilization back into a dark age. Divis Mal helped found Aeon, back in the 1920s. . . only to see it turn into a society of monsters. Monsters who've convinced the world that they're here to help.<br /> <br /> (Yep, that's right - the bad guys won the Aberrant War. Hate to disillusion anyone)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=183043#post183043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Teragen book, while discussing &quot;The Night of Long Knives.&quot; And on the note of Trinity, Divis Mal is MENTIONED, like a boogeyman, but never actually appears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure about that? I pulled the <i>Teragen</i> book to look up the rules for Chrysalis, and a lot of that just isn't there. Maybe in one of the <i>Phase</i> books, instead?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T22:56:55-07:00","id":463158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=462023#post462023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of Divis Mal's deal is that he's been through the Chrysalis multiple times - which results in cumulative penalties to understand or socialize with mundane humans. Assuming the count in the <i>Teragen</i> book is accurate, and he entered chrysalis at the minimum levels each time, he's got <i>at least</i> a +3 penalty (i.e. base difficulty of 10) to any social roll involving baselines. As others have pointed out, he just doesn't think like mundane humans any more, and that limits his ability to anticipate their reactions, or have normal, healthy relationships with them (and that's before including any possible mental aberrations he may suffer). Heck, the <i>Teragen</i> book implies that he's having problems maintaining normal relationships with other novas!<br /> <br /> Another big aspect of his personality (and subsequent dealings with the world) is that Divis Mal seems to have been deeply influenced by Nietzsche. If you've never read Nietzsche, his work basically postulates that modern standards of good and evil have been corrupted and subverted by the elites/one percenters/powers-that-be into concepts that merely uphold the status quo, and keeping themselves in power. But Nietzsche also postulated that the time was right for a &quot;superhuman&quot; (ubermensch), someone who would defy such labels, overthrow the status quo, and open a new dawn of possibilities to the world. Sound familiar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I've been putting off reading reading Nietzsche in favor of Machiavelli's The Prince, but now I have to read Nietzsche. I'm assuming the Ubermensch postulate is in <i>Men and Supermen</i>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=462023#post462023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in the Aeon Society, Mal probably sees those beliefs (about the corruption of &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot;) firmly validated. Sure, Aeon is backing Project Utopia . . . .but they're also firmly supporting Project Proteus. And Proteus . . . wow, they're into some seriously evil things. Assassinations and black sites. Kidnapping and torture. Raping female novas, so that Project Proteus scientists can dissect the kids to see what second generation novas will be like. During the time of <i>Aberrant</i>, Aeon is effectively the Red Cross - just with death camps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit. I haven't read too deeply into the Aeonverse books (I'm only going to call the Aeon/Aberrant/Adventure books published from now on as the Trinity Continuum books, with everything previously published as Aeonverse books), but I knew about Proteus being behind the conspiracy to murder Slider. I knew about the unknowing sterilization of novas to prevent them from breeding more novas. But Proteus deliberately raping female novas and harvesting the resulting babies for <i>vivisection</i>? Forgive the violation of Godwin's Law, but that sick shit is right out of Nazi Germany. That's not just the Red Cross with death camps....That's the Red Cross with death camps <i>and </i>rape camps. Jesus Christ, no wonder the novas went on a Roaring Rampage of Revenge during the Aberrant War. I mean, even without <i>that</i>, the Aberrant War already seems inevitable, but <i>with </i>that...wow.<br /> <br /> And heaven help Aeon if the psiads ever find out about this. And despite Proteus destroying all their records and whitewashing the history of the Aberrant Era, that eventuality is <i>not </i>impossible. Correct me if I'm wrong, but The Colony was around during the Aberrant War, wasn't he? I remember reading somewhere that some people in Trinity were speculating that if The Colony had returned from deep space, then Divis Mal might still be around as well (even though Word of God says that Divis Mal is not coming back). Given that some novas are, compared to humans, very long-lived, then The Colony <i>can't</i> be the only nova alive in Trinity from the Aberrant era. How many of the Eden novas lived through the Aberrant War and still remember what Proteus did to them and their friends? How many of them told their descendants and their baseline followers? How long before an Upeo Wa Macho or some other psiad offhandedly mentions the Aeon Trinity to an Edenite and the Edenite goes &quot;Wait wait wait...the Aeon Society is <i>still around</i>? Do you know what those baby butchers <i>did </i>to us?&quot; How long before an Edenite tells a psiad the <i>real </i>history of the Aberrant War and then says,&quot;They came for us in the night because they were scared shitless of us and our superhuman powers. <i>You've</i> got superhuman powers. How long before they begin to fear you? How long before they come for <i>you</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=462023#post462023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no one seems to care. When Corbin finally gets hard proof about Proteus, the UN turns him over . . . .to the Aeon Society. Later, during the Aberrant War, Aeon endorses the genocide of anyone related to novas (even former Project Utopia members), and destroys all nova-based research it can find, plunging civilization back into a dark age. Divis Mal helped found Aeon, back in the 1920s. . . only to see it turn into a society of monsters. Monsters who've convinced the world that they're here to help.<br /> <br /> (Yep, that's right - the bad guys won the Aberrant War. Hate to disillusion anyone.)</div> </div> </div> </div>And what shocks me the most about all this is that Mercer, the leading founder of the Aeon Society, very likely foresaw all of this with his Timey Wimey Ball powers <i>and let it happen</i>. And the only reason a man like Mercer would have stood by and let all this happen is because any intervention on his part would have led to something <i>worse</i>.<br /> <br /> Just what the fuck did Mercer see to make him stand by and let World War II, the Holocaust, Proteus' atrocities, the Aberrant War <i>and </i>the Crash happen on his watch? What could be worse than all that? Did he somehow realize that if he tried to prevent all this, he'd somehow trigger the extinction of the human race?<br /> <br /> <i>What did Mercer see?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 03-31-2015, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T05:58:27-07:00","id":463376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463158#post463158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming the Ubermensch postulate is in <i>Men and Supermen</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not read it, but i'm pretty sure you won't be finding the real meat in GB Shaw's musings on the subject - however entertaining or contemporary.<br /> -tease-<br /> &quot;<i>Thus spoke Zarathustra</i>&quot; is the place to start for Ubermenschen. He may bring it up again elsewhere (i'm looking at you &quot;<i>Beyond Good and Evil</i>&quot;), but as convincing as he sounds to me personally , i lack the background in philosophy and German to really speak authoritatively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463158#post463158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit. I haven't read too deeply into the Aeonverse books (I'm only going to call the Aeon/Aberrant/Adventure books published from now on as the Trinity Continuum books, with everything previously published as Aeonverse books), but I knew about Proteus being behind the conspiracy to murder Slider. I knew about the unknowing sterilization of novas to prevent them from breeding more novas. But Proteus deliberately raping female novas and harvesting the resulting babies for <i>vivisection</i>? Forgive the violation of Godwin's Law, but that sick shit is right out of Nazi Germany. That's not just the Red Cross with death camps....That's the Red Cross with death camps <i>and </i>rape camps. Jesus Christ, no wonder the novas went on a Roaring Rampage of Revenge during the Aberrant War. I mean, even without <i>that</i>, the Aberrant War already seems inevitable, but <i>with </i>that...wow.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my few objections to this reaction is really how ham-fisted it came off in retrospective. Since the Godwin threshold now lies in the past of this thread, the Society had lived through the holocaust and may have even supported the &quot;wrong&quot; side there too - i can see elements of Nazi Walt Disney being present in early Max - although it's never really given much weight next to the trumpets of two-fisted crimefighting and other philanthropy. Perhaps a demonstration of Germanic Inspired left a national fervor that spun out of control during the harsh years following the Great War, perhaps the Society learned many harsh lessons during this time leading up to the battle with Primoris. I would draw similarities with modern Israeli history, and hope nobody takes it as an insult, both are organizations scarred by those calamitious events in the 1930s and 40s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463158#post463158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And heaven help Aeon if the psiads ever find out about this. And despite Proteus destroying all their records and whitewashing the history of the Aberrant Era, that eventuality is <i>not </i>impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throw in Prometheus chamber Clairsentients scheduled to start popping up, undiscovered and sufficiently isolated war era databases, living memory and other elements - i get the impression by 2120 that it's only the naive and younger generations that actually buy the Neptune Division party line out of Aeon. But there isn't any other solid information to dispute it with by that stage - it's very Orwellian for an organization that claims to be benevolent. I'm really looking forward to see what the Onyx Path guys are going to do about these conflictions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463158#post463158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong, but The Colony was around during the Aberrant War, wasn't he?</div> </div> </div> </div>I spent a lot of time trying to find anything to confirm this, but the Colony as a person/actor/NPC is never mentioned in any capacity together with the Aberrant War era. I tried to infer greater significance from what little IS said from his return in the 2100s and came up with more from the Battle Ground material (disagreement with Kali/Yog Death) than from the RPG stuff. If anyone knows better please shoot me down, i've been stuck up here for nearly a decade. -smile-<br /> The fact that everyone seems to know who he is (on the same hand-wavey level that we know Wycroft, Birlesme and of course Divis Mal by name), is the only actual evidence i've ever found in the 2120 setting that the Colony isn't some unknown 2nd/3rd gen space-born squid. I remember having parts pointed out from the Aberrant setting excitedly by my brother, but none ever really jumped out at me as candidates - except maybe Buendia - but that's really a question for another thread.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463158#post463158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading somewhere that some people in Trinity were speculating that if The Colony had returned from deep space, then Divis Mal might still be around as well (even though Word of God says that Divis Mal is not coming back). Given that some novas are, compared to humans, very long-lived, then The Colony <i>can't</i> be the only nova alive in Trinity from the Aberrant era. How many of the Eden novas lived through the Aberrant War and still remember what Proteus did to them and their friends? How many of them told their descendants and their baseline followers? How long before an Upeo Wa Macho or some other psiad offhandedly mentions the Aeon Trinity to an Edenite and the Edenite goes &quot;Wait wait wait...the Aeon Society is <i>still around</i>? Do you know what those baby butchers <i>did </i>to us?&quot; How long before an Edenite tells a psiad the <i>real </i>history of the Aberrant War and then says,&quot;They came for us in the night because they were scared shitless of us and our superhuman powers. <i>You've</i> got superhuman powers. How long before they begin to fear you? How long before they come for <i>you</i>?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of personally irritates me that 2120 got stripped of a complex character like Donighal, in favor of a 2d cartoon villain like the Colony - where was the fun in that? Mal explicitly promises that return in his final address to the UN (admittedly not mentioning he will play any part), leaving the drama between he and Mercer criminally unresolved. Then in Stellar Frontiers we get Apollo Milliken who seems to be (unironically) operating out of black and whites as well, despite having a few very tasty moral conflicts concerning aberrants in between the lines of DR's Huang-Marr project - all in all the 2120 setting required DM mandate/vision for the varied depictions to really gel. -shrug-<br /> We are missing decades from the war narrative. I fully expected the 'lost years' to be sidling up to the silver age of comics and seeing mass hysteria, confusion and ignorance being manipulated seperately from many flashpoints - Proteus is likely severely castrated by the Aberrant group in the early 30s or so in my mind and only makes a come-back in the do or die years of the war and becomes enough of a symbol to be integrated into the Trinity. Fear of 'Novas' becomes inborn to the humans of those generations and later, greatly devoid of the hopefulness that characterized the initial years. To the later Novas, humanity will seem increasingly like animals or cattle. By the time 2049 rolls around and the seminal events of the official war begin, that next generation is beginning to make decisions entirely divorced from the culture of the 2008 setting.<br /> Proteus may have served as a banner for human stewardship of the future of earth, in a tale of redemption or entrenched corruption, depending on your take on the setting. But honestly, to my taste, they went a little too far for redemption and are very likely tolerated strictly as a servile component of the Trinity - which might go some way to sequestering their atrocities from the greater Aeon society - to which they were never directly attached (painstakingly at times, iirc).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463158#post463158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what shocks me the most about all this is that Mercer, the leading founder of the Aeon Society, very likely foresaw all of this with his Timey Wimey Ball powers <i>and let it happen</i>. And the only reason a man like Mercer would have stood by and let all this happen is because any intervention on his part would have led to something <i>worse</i>.<br /> <br /> Just what the fuck did Mercer see to make him stand by and let World War II, the Holocaust, Proteus' atrocities, the Aberrant War <i>and </i>the Crash happen on his watch? What could be worse than all that? Did he somehow realize that if he tried to prevent all this, he'd somehow trigger the extinction of the human race?<br /> <br /> <i>What did Mercer see?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This deserves a thread all of it's own. I've started my own fair share of late if anyone else wants to get that started, prior to me overcoming my laziness to do it myself. As others have mentioned earlier in this thread, Max prefers a hands-off approach and <i>may</i> not have acted to stop any of them, even <i>if</i> he could.<br /> Mercers time travel would have to be given some kind of parameters for any discussion of his actual capabilities to get off the ground, we never really found out if he could change things within the single timeline, create new parrallel time-branches or was solidly stapled to fatalism.<br /> Seriously, start that thread and i shall have much to query - Max has a slippery capacity to play as many roles in the metaplot as he has disguises. He inevitably comes up when Donighal does, but the two have many mysteries entirely detached of each other.<br /> Good questions, Su-tehp, hopefully Lustral Star's planned exposition on his 200 year campaign will be as incisive on Mercer as he was on Donighal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Can't believe i forgot 'Beyond good and evil'... 04-18-2015, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T01:34:41-07:00","id":464406,"title":"","content":"This post took me at least 2 hours to compose, and I did it at 3 in the morning. I'm either crazy, am suffering from <i>extreme </i>insomnia or have entirely too much time on my hands. Probably all of the above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463376#post463376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not read [Men and Supermen], but I\u2019m pretty sure you won't be finding the real meat in GB Shaw's musings on the subject - however entertaining or contemporary.<br /> -tease-<br /> &quot;<i>Thus spoke Zarathustra</i>&quot; is the place to start and finish for Ubermenschen. He may bring it up again elsewhere, but as convincing as he sounds to me personally , I lack the background in philosophy and German to really speak authoritatively. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is my fault. I vaguely remembered the title Men and Supermen from somewhere and thought it was one of Nietzsche\u2019s works. The truth of the matter was only a few Internet clicks away and I was too lazy to do so. So I fully admit I deserved the tease.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463376#post463376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my few objections to this reaction is really how ham-fisted it came off in retrospect. Since the Godwin threshold now lies in the past of this thread, the Society had lived through the holocaust and may have even supported the &quot;wrong&quot; side there too - I can see elements of Nazi Walt Disney being present in early Max - although it's never really given much weight next to the trumpets of two-fisted crimefighting and other philanthropy. Perhaps a demonstration of Germanic Inspired left a national fervor that spun out of control during the harsh years following the Great War, perhaps the Society learned many harsh lessons during this time leading up to the battle with Primoris. I would draw similarities with modern Israeli history, and hope nobody takes it as an insult, both are organizations scarred by those calamitous events in the 1930s and 40s.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you say \u201cone of my few objections to this reaction is really how ham-fisted it came off in retrospect,\u201d did you mean my own reaction of comparing the Proteus vivisection of 2nd generation nova infants and the rape of their mothers to Nazi Germany? Given that the dictionary definition of \u201cham-fisted\u201d means \u201cclumsy or awkward,\u201d I can totally see how my visceral reaction to the idea of infants that were the result of rape being vivisected could come off as awkward. But then, Rape is a Special Kind of Evil, as TVTropes says. And I did knowingly and deliberately invoke/violate Godwin\u2019s Law, which perhaps only added to the awkwardness. Invoking Nazi Germany is something that people do to emphasize the idea of \u201cultimate evil.\u201d But invoking Nazi Germany is something that is very easily abused; that\u2019s why Godwin\u2019s law exists, as we all know. So was my instinctive and visceral reaction ham-fisted in retrospect? I suppose I can see that. But then again, one would have to be at least sociopathic (if not outright psychopathic) to not find the idea of rape camps and infant vivisection (even in a fictional setting) at least somewhat disturbing. Nonetheless, I did violate Godwin\u2019s law deliberately and knowingly, so any awkwardness that ensued here is, I think, my responsibility.<br /> <br /> If I misunderstood your meaning, I await your clarification at your convenience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463376#post463376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throw in Prometheus chamber Clairsentients scheduled to start popping up, undiscovered and sufficiently isolated war era databases, living memory and other elements - I get the impression by 2120 that it's only the naive and younger generations that actually buy the Neptune Division party line out of Aeon. But there isn't any other solid information to dispute it with by that stage - it's very Orwellian for an organization that claims to be benevolent. I'm really looking forward to see what the Onyx Path guys are going to do about these conflictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m very eager to see how this works out as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463376#post463376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kind of personally irritates me that 2120 got stripped of a complex character like Donighal, in favor of a 2d cartoon villain like the Colony - where was the fun in that? Mal explicitly promises that return in his final address to the UN (admittedly not mentioning he will play any part), leaving the drama between he and Mercer criminally unresolved. Then in Stellar Frontiers we get Apollo Milliken who seems to be (unironically) operating out of black and whites as well, despite having a few very tasty moral conflicts concerning Aberrants in between the lines of DR's Huang-Marr project - all in all the 2120 setting required DM mandate/vision for the varied depictions to really gel. -shrug-<br /> We are missing decades from the war narrative. I fully expected the 'lost years' to be sidling up to the silver age of comics and seeing mass hysteria, confusion and ignorance being manipulated separately from many flashpoints - Proteus is likely severely castrated by the Aberrant group in the early 30s or so in my mind and only makes a come-back in the do or die years of the war and becomes enough of a symbol to be integrated into the Trinity. Fear of 'Novas' becomes inborn to the humans of those generations and later, greatly devoid of the hopefulness that characterized the initial years. To the later Novas, humanity will seem increasingly like animals or cattle. By the time 2049 rolls around and the seminal events of the official war begin, that next generation is beginning to make decisions entirely divorced from the culture of the 2008 setting.<br /> Proteus may have served as a banner for human stewardship of the future of earth, in a tale of redemption or entrenched corruption, depending on your take on the setting. But honestly, to my taste, they went a little too far for redemption and are very likely tolerated strictly as a servile component of the Trinity - which might go some way to sequestering their atrocities from the greater Aeon society - to which they were never directly attached (painstakingly at times, iirc).</div> </div> </div> </div>This +100. I also was very disappointed that Trinity got stripped of Divis Mal. I just took a few peeks at both the Trinity Storytellers Guide PDF and some of the letters between Donighal and Mercer in the Adventure corebook that Lustral Star references in his posts. Very heady stuff. And I totally agree with you about how this huge dramatic conflict over the destiny of the human race between Mercer and Divis Mal was being set up\u2026and then Word of God says that Divis Mal is gone and never coming back. Wait, what? At the end of the Aberrant War, Divis Mal says \u201cyour legacy is our future,\u201d all but saying \u201cpitiful mortals, I\u2019ll be back\u2026\u201d and then he never comes back? What kind of villain swears revenge and then never shows up again? And with Divis Mal being such a complicated character with actual, plausible reasons for his Start of Darkness being replaced by The Colony, a 2-dimensional, only-mentioned-offscreen villain? Yeah, I agree with you, Nihilist; this is utterly negligent from a storywise perspective. Granted, I\u2019m no writer (although I want to learn how to be a novelist one day), but Divis Mal just abandoning his thirst for vengeance against humanity feels like a cop-out, even if he does supposedly have the ability to create a new universe where he could rule as a god-king.<br /> <br /> I can understand from a story perspective of the Trinity devs wanting to keep the focus on the PCs, and maybe that\u2019s why they wanted to get rid of Divis Mal so that his conflict with Mercer over humanity\u2019s destiny doesn\u2019t overshadow the story about the player characters. But just having a believable and complicated and authentic Big Bad like Divis Mal suddenly saying \u201cScrew This, I\u2019m Outta Here!\u201d after sitting in the lotus position on an airless asteroid for 50 years contemplating humanity\u2019s destiny as well as his own and whether they should have anything to do with each other feels like a cop-out the size of the Virgo Supercluster (roughly 100 million light-years across).<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t see an authentic villain like Divis Mal saying \u201cI will rule mankind\u2019s destiny because might makes right! I am FIRST among Homo Sapiens Novus and humanity\u2019s legacy is my future--Eh? What\u2019s this? I can create an entirely new universe where I can create its own physical laws and rule as a god-king for ever and ever and ever? Cool! I wanna see!\u201d and then Divis Mal, with a childlike grin that almost seems to split his face in half, leaps headfirst into a trans-universal glowy portal thingie and is never seen again.<br /> <br /> WTF?<br /> <br /> Seriously, WTF.<br /> <br /> I mean, I know gods (and godlike entities) are notorious for being capricious and arbitrary, but having Divis Mal, given all the complexities and humanity (and transhumanism?) he has, suddenly suffering the biggest case of ADHD in the universe to distract him from his own (self-deluded) quest to control mankind's destiny just <i>doesn't make any sense</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463376#post463376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This [Mercer\u2019s reasons for not preventing the atrocities of the 20<sup>th</sup> Century and the Aberrant Era] deserves a thread all of its own. I've started my own fair share of late if anyone else wants to get that started, prior to me overcoming my laziness to do it myself. As others have mentioned earlier in this thread, Max prefers a hands-off approach and <i>may</i> not have acted to stop any of them, even <i>if</i> he could.<br /> Mercers time travel would have to be given some kind of parameters for any discussion of his actual capabilities to get off the ground, we never really found out if he could change things within the single timeline, create new parallel time-branches or was solidly stapled to fatalism.<br /> Seriously, start that thread and I shall have much to query - Max has a slippery capacity to play as many roles in the metaplot as he has disguises. He inevitably comes up when Donighal does, but the two have many mysteries entirely detached of each other.<br /> Good questions, Su-tehp, hopefully Lustral Star's planned exposition on his 200 year campaign will be as insightful on Mercer as he was on Donighal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, Nihilist. I admit that I\u2019m not as a big a fan of, or as knowledgeable of, the Aeonverse as I am of the oWoD, but I try to keep up with the basics of Trinity. It is a great game, after all. And I\u2019m eager to see what Lustral Star\u2019s insights on Mercer are as well.<br /> <br /> It turns out that the Trinity Storytellers Guide PDF does tell the story of Mercer\u2019s time travel resulting from the Hammersmith Incident, but it gets\u2026weird. If I understood it correctly, apparently when Mercer reached 2122, he was somehow\u2026bifurcated when he reached the Venezuela Event. So now there are two of him, one that saw mankind\u2019s future beyond 2122 and one that\u2026didn\u2019t. And as a result, the Mercer that didn\u2019t see past 2122 wound up drawing all the wrong conclusions.<br /> <br /> Like I said, weird.<br /> <br /> Does this mean that instead of Mercer having this great thematically inspired conflict over humanity\u2019s destiny with Divis Mal, he\u2019ll instead be having the conflict with\u2026his magically created, Well-Intentioned-Extremist twin?<br /> <br /> *sound of violent gagging, immediately followed by sound of chunky industrial waste puke falling into (and slightly missing) the nearest toilet*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 04-01-2015, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T05:33:25-07:00","id":464600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464406#post464406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This post took me at least 2 hours to compose, and I did it at 3 in the morning. I'm either crazy, am suffering from <i>extreme </i>insomnia or have entirely too much time on my hands. Probably all of the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clinical insomnia evidently leads to overthinking and at times over posting, i'm personally well aware of this. I can attest, at least, that you aren't the only sufferer.<br /> -tired smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464406#post464406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you say \u201cone of my few objections to this reaction is really how ham-fisted it came off in retrospect,\u201d did you mean my own reaction of comparing the Proteus vivisection of 2nd generation nova infants and the rape of their mothers to Nazi Germany?<br /> <br /> If I misunderstood your meaning, I await your clarification at your convenience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, time for me to accept some responsibility too.<br /> That first line should have been properly expanded; i am not a fan of how obviously, &quot;ham-fistedly&quot; evil Proteus comes off in the 2008 narrative. I treasure my grey scales and clear Good/Evil in any white-wolf sourced material wasn't what i was buying it for. Surely an organization with this many good thinkers could come up with something more subtle, i think. Where is the PR spin and the misconceptions that drip off the rest of the setting?<br /> On your part, any discussion about Mercer v Primoris is eventually going to end up crossing the Godwin threshold - no foul. Nothing i can remember from the source material suggests WW2 doesn't occur as it does in our own history, eventually Aeon itself violates Godwin. Your defense is strong, so i'm glad you pulled me up there and even gladder i could honestly backpedal from the remark in relations to your reaction (as opposed to Proteus').<br /> ...<br /> Rape IS a special kind of evil as far as fiction is concerned at least, i don't like to deal with it in game (how would you even... -ick-), but i <i>can</i> use it as background <i>sometimes</i>.<br /> I may 'be at least sociopathic (if not outright psychopathic)' but i retain enough nerve endings to also be repulsed by such things, i only take issue with the fervency which Proteus was demonized with at times. Beyond that; i would have to defend rape, even if only as a purely fictional dramatic device - that's not a conversation i'm interested in pursuing. I can't even remember where it comes up in the 2008 source, to be completely honest. I'd ask One Vorlon to point it out, if i didn't already feel like i was so far off topic.<br /> ...<br /> Apologies for the misunderstanding, Su-tehp. You would stand righteously victorious had we actually been disagreeing on anything.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464406#post464406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This +100.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome rant, Su-tehp. You put a very fine point on that arguement for the next time i whip it out. I've neglected to quote all your lamentations (although i was tempted, for truth), but i feel we are on the same page.<br /> Dramatically, this is one of the meta-plot's greatest failures. Either climax in the Aberrant War (which could have happened, but how would the fans even know?), or leave the tangent in, i say.<br /> Again, interested to see Lustral Star's approach here, he's told me that he'll try to get us an outline through the easter break. I hope he finds the time, with all due respect to RL.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464406#post464406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">feels like a cop-out the size of the Virgo Supercluster (roughly 100 million light-years across).</div> </div> </div> </div>-standing ovation-<br /> Nice contextual use of the Virgo supercluster, that makes for an alarmingly sizeable 'cop-out'.<br /> I agree with this statement, but in a gaming sense, sequestering Donighal/Mal is fine, he spent most of the previous two settings sequestered anyway (where any good Deus Ex Machina should remain during most stories). But this was just an unofficial tidbit in the end, unpublished 'Word of God' can also be seen as heresy unless it gets locked down in the text. I took it to mean simply; &quot;Divis Mal will never show up in our published supplements for 2120&quot;. Which still leaves the meta-plot unceremoniously severed on that front, for reasons i've never really understood - glad to see i'm not alone.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464406#post464406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, Nihilist. I admit that I\u2019m not as a big a fan of, or as knowledgeable of, the Aeonverse as I am of the oWoD, but I try to keep up with the basics of Trinity. It is a great game, after all. And I\u2019m eager to see what Lustral Star\u2019s insights on Mercer are as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>oWoD? Cool, i think we're operating off the same fanbase then. You still seem to know your Aeon well enough to dive in the deep end of a Primoris/Mal debate, which is <i>pretty well</i> last time i checked - you must know the hell out of oWoD.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464406#post464406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It turns out that the Trinity Storytellers Guide PDF does tell the story of Mercer\u2019s time travel resulting from the Hammersmith Incident, but it gets\u2026weird. If I understood it correctly, apparently when Mercer reached 2122, he was somehow\u2026bifurcated when he reached the Venezuela Event. So now there are two of him, one that saw mankind\u2019s future beyond 2122 and one that\u2026didn\u2019t. And as a result, the Mercer that didn\u2019t see past 2122 wound up drawing all the wrong conclusions.<br /> <br /> Like I said, weird.<br /> <br /> Does this mean that instead of Mercer having this great thematically inspired conflict over humanity\u2019s destiny with Divis Mal, he\u2019ll instead be having the conflict with\u2026his magically created, Well-Intentioned-Extremist twin?<br /> <br /> *sound of violent gagging, immediately followed by sound of chunky industrial waste puke falling into (and slightly missing) the nearest toilet*</div> </div> </div> </div>-sidesteps violent regurgitations, pities janitors-<br /> Yeah, that is a little wierd, but adding time travel to an all but finished product is a metric shit-ton of work for an author - which is why i always held out hope that the original devs had some secret solution left unpublished somewhere - because time travel kind of <i>needs</i> to be written in from step one forward. But this isn't to cast aspersions over the creative and ambitious work that led that title to the point it reached, they were operating without any real framework and did a hell of a job given the limitations inherent to the project.<br /> But, the time travel part didn't quite hit the right tone for me either - its matter-of-fact inclusion, however, is one of the facts i can point to hopefully for the new editions.<br /> Otherwise, i really have to insist we get a new thread started about Max/time-travel to continue that examination - i can easily baloon out a few hundred or thousand words there if i get started.<br /> -shame-<br /> Great posts, Su-tehp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T14:15:57-07:00","id":465160,"title":"","content":"Ok, this post took me <i>all afternoon</i> to compose. Here goes...<br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to respond to a couple of things first out of order because they need to get cleared up straightaway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464600#post464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may 'be at least sociopathic (if not outright psychopathic)' but i retain enough nerve endings to also be repulsed by such things, i only take issue with the fervency which Proteus was demonized with at times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, <i>ouch</i>. Nihilist, I didn\u2019t mean to imply you to be a sociopath or psychopath <i>at all</i>. In fact, that\u2019s why I specifically decided to use the phrase \u201cone would have to be sociopathic\u2026\u201d rather than \u201cyou\u2019d have to be sociopathic\u2026\u201d with the \u201cyou\u201d in that phrase being meant to mean \u201ceveryone in general\u201d for just this reason: I didn\u2019t want to you to misunderstand me into thinking I was calling you a psychopath. As I\u2019ve never even met you in person, insulting your sanity would be in very poor taste. Yes, many flame wars have started for <i>far</i> less, but everyone on this forum has a vested interest in keeping things civil. No insult or even implication of you being a sociopath or psychopath was intended, Nihilist. I just want to make sure you understand this.<br /> <br /> In any event, if a 3<sup>rd</sup> party mental health profession were to examine you in my presence and loudly come to the conclusion that \u201cTHIS GUY\u2019S BUGFUCK CRAZY!!!!\u201d I would, in good conscience, have to say: \u201cI don\u2019t know if Nihilist meant his handle to be a literal statement on his mental outlook, but regardless, he\u2019s always been nice to <i>me</i>\u2026.\u201d <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464600#post464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rape IS a special kind of evil as far as fiction is concerned at least, i don't like to deal with it in game (how would you even... -ick-), but i <i>can</i> use it as background <i>sometimes</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is the whole reason that White Wolf games are \u201cFor Mature Minds,\u201d after all. Any subject this touchy in a roleplaying game needs to be handled <i>very</i> carefully and it\u2019s good to see White Wolf as a company owning up to their responsibility on this. (Corporate responsibility, yay! More, please.)<br /> <br /> Ok, now back to our regularly scheduled program.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464600#post464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oops, time for me to accept some responsibility too. That first line should have been properly expanded; i am not a fan of how obviously, &quot;ham-fistedly&quot; evil Proteus comes off in the 2008 narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh you were talking about <i>Proteus\u2019</i> reaction to Slider\u2019s investigation of their conspiracy when you used the phrase \u201cone of my few objections to this reaction is really how ham-fisted it came off in retrospect\u2026.\u201d Either that or you were referring to Proteus\u2019 \u201cmedical experiments\u201d on novas as a reaction to the implied threat novas posed to the human race.<br /> <br /> I thought you were talking about my visceral reaction of disgust upon finding out about Proteus\u2019 human vivisection of nova infants. Ok, that\u2019s what threw me off.<br /> <br /> As for Proteus\u2019 sloppy elimination of Slider, it does make sense from a narrative perspective that unanticipated errors or accidents will usually expose a conspiracy. By their very nature, conspirators have to be <i>exceptionally</i> meticulous to keep their agendas hidden. But accidents happen and mistakes are made\u2026and when conspiracies are in sudden danger of being exposed, the conspirators usually (and expectedly) begin to panic. And when they panic, they make even more mistakes which leads to more chances of exposing their conspiracy and the whole thing snowballs\u2026. Add to this the fact that the mistake that started the whole mess was Proteus sending Chiraben, of all its agents, to kill Slider. <i>Chiraben</i>. A known psychopath who didn\u2019t even bother trying to Make It Look Like An Accident.<br /> <br /> After that, it was inevitable (in-story) that the human solid waste excrement would hit the electrically-powered oscillating unit.<br /> <br /> My own opinion is that Proteus\u2019 panic in reaction to the danger Slider posed to their conspiracy isn\u2019t hand-fisted at all, but flows right into conventional conspiracy tropes. I might call it conventional (or, if I wanted to be unkind, derivative or unoriginal), but as it is a tried-and-true trope, I can\u2019t call it ham-fisted or clumsy <i>per se</i> from a story/narrative perspective. Even its conventionality isn\u2019t necessarily a bad thing; lots of works borrow ideas from other works and are much better for it. Using conventional conspiracy tropes in a game that involves political intrigue is, to my mind, an absolute necessity. The story of Aberrant wouldn\u2019t make sense otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464600#post464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> oWoD? Cool, i think we're operating off the same fanbase then. You still seem to know your Aeon well enough to dive in the deep end of a Primoris/Mal debate, which is <i>pretty well</i> last time i checked - you must know the hell out of oWoD.<br /> -smile-</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I remember more than a little bit about Trinity, a little less about Aberrant and almost nothing at all (until last night) about Adventure. Hell, last night, when I read the letters between Mercer and Donighal, was the first time I opened the Adventure corebook since I first bought it! (Not surprising, really; I\u2019m far more a fan of sci-fi than I am of pulp fiction. I just bought Adventure \u201cfor the collection\u201d and because it was the first part of the Aeon metaplot.)<br /> <br /> As for my knowledge of the oWoD, I must have what is quite probably one of the most (if not the most) complete collections of first print oWoD books on the East Coast. It fills at least a full bookcase and a half in my apartment. (Benefits of having a rich [or at least <i>very</i> well-to-do] and generous father.) Granted, I haven\u2019t read a lot of those books cover-to-cover, but they have been quite informative. That collection (not just of White Wolf books, but <i>all </i>my RPG books) is my most prized material possession, bar none.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464600#post464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> -sidesteps violent regurgitations, pities janitors-</div> </div> </div> </div>I salute you on your agility <i>and</i> your empathy, sir. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464600#post464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, [Trinity ST Handbook\u2019s account of Mercer\u2019s time travel] is a little wierd, but adding time travel to an all but finished product is a metric shit-ton of work for an author - which is why i always held out hope that the original devs had some secret solution left unpublished somewhere - because time travel kind of <i>needs</i> to be written in from step one forward. But this isn't to cast aspersions over the creative and ambitious work that led that title to the point it reached, they were operating without any real framework and did a hell of a job given the limitations inherent to the project.<br /> But, the time travel part didn't quite hit the right tone for me either - its matter-of-fact inclusion, however, is one of the facts i can point to hopefully for the new editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Time travel tropes (especially in Star Trek!) have almost always annoyed me unless they are <i>very</i> meticulously planned out ahead of time. You said that they need to be planned out at least one step ahead of time; I\u2019d argue that they need to be planned out at least three or four steps ahead. (The space-time continuum tends to, y\u2019know, <i>continue</i> when you consider that the universe is <i>14 billion years old</i>. That\u2019s a lot of continuing.) And this is a nigh-Herculean task. I give props to the Trinity devs for attempting it, especially since it\u2019s so central to Mercer\u2019s story. But it\u2019s very easy to screw up and derail the story.<br /> <br /> And you\u2019re right about the TSTHB account of Mercer\u2019s time travel not hitting the right tone; it didn\u2019t for me either, but then again, it <i>is</i> an unfinished product. I\u2019m eager to see what the Trinity devs do with this now that they have the chance to go back and tell Trinity\u2019s story again. It might be years before we know anything for sure, but as long as it\u2019s done right, it will be worth the wait.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464600#post464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Otherwise, i really have to insist we get a new thread started about Max/time-travel to continue that examination - i can easily balloon out a few hundred or thousand words there if i get started.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don\u2019t think I can in good conscience start this thread either, at least not yet. Maybe soon, though. We'll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464600#post464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> -shame-</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, don\u2019t feel bad. If you balloon out a few hundred words, and then if I balloon out a few hundred words and then if Lustral Star balloons out a few hundred words\u2026maybe, just maybe, we\u2019ll catch something the devs missed and Ian will grace us with his presence here in the forums again and it\u2019ll be one more contribution that makes the Trinity Continuum even better. Nothing to feel ashamed about there. Sometimes Sesquipedalian Loquaciousness can work to everyone\u2019s advantage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464600#post464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Great posts, Su-tehp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 04-01-2015, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T20:46:31-07:00","id":465562,"title":"","content":"The story of Mercer's time travel which I put in the ST Handbook was something developed by the original crew; I think Elizabeth D. Brooks was specifically the one who came up with it, but Bruce agreed with it. Part of my goal with the STH was to take a lot of these bits which the team had planned and discussed and put them in a public place for the fans to use.<br /> <br /> While the flashpoint was the Venezuelan Phenomenon, remember that Max can only (or at least &quot;most easily&quot;) travel to periods with a substantial amount of subquantum flux: most notably the Hammersmith event, WWII, N-Day, the end of the Aberrant War, and the Venezuelan Phenomenon. So jumping forward from the Aberrant War to get a peek at humanity's future, he bifurcates: one lands in the 2120s as expected, sees humanity prospering, and returns to his own time to found a more peaceful, hopeful Aeon Society, as depicted in Adventure! and Trinity. The other Max bounces back, and comes to the conclusion that the trip failed because the world has been destroyed. He creates a more pessimistic Aeon, more geared toward damage control, as depicted in Aberrant.<br /> <br /> So ultimately it was just a way to explain why the Aeon Societies of Adventure!/Trinity and Aberrant seem very different, when ostensibly Max is still in charge either directly or indirectly in every era. When your founder can time travel, you expect that if your organization is up to some shifty business, the founder will ultimately know about it. If he doesn't stop you, it must be because he approves -- or even started the shifty business in the first place.<br /> <br /> Now with the Trinity Continuum, things work sufficiently differently that we won't need to rely on this explanation. Aeon will be more cohesive throughout each era, the flashpoints are different, and time travel doesn't work exactly the same because of reasons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T04:49:29-07:00","id":465921,"title":"","content":"Dammit, Ian, just when i think i extracted myself from clogging this thread with Time-travelling Max Mercer, you've pulled me back in!<br /> -shakes fist melodramatically-<br /> <br /> I've been driven to create a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/465988-max-mercer-what-s-his-deal\">new discussion thread</a> for this purpose...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Added thread and link. 04-02-2015, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T09:35:35-07:00","id":466215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=465562#post465562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So ultimately [Mercer's bifurcated time travel] was just a way to explain why the Aeon Societies of Adventure!/Trinity and Aberrant seem very different, when ostensibly Max is still in charge either directly or indirectly in every era. When your founder can time travel, you expect that if your organization is up to some shifty business, the founder will ultimately know about it. If he doesn't stop you, it must be because he approves -- or even started the shifty business in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the idea of there being two Mercers running around working at cross purposes throughout the Aeon story just struck me as...clunky. Do the two Mercers even know of each other's existence? Did they create two separate Aeon Societies in 1923? Or did the Mercer who bounced back from the Aberrant War thinking the world was destroyed merely land in 2008 and remade/reorganized the Aeon Society that was already in existence which had been created by his &quot;good twin?&quot; This explanation never made much sense to me.<br /> <br /> By the way, my above questions are rhetorical; there's no need to try to answer them here. I will likely ask them again in the proper thread (see below).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=465562#post465562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now with the Trinity Continuum, things work sufficiently differently that we won't need to rely on this explanation. Aeon will be more cohesive throughout each era, the flashpoints are different, and time travel doesn't work exactly the same because of reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank the gawds. I can't wait to see the final result. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=465921#post465921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dammit, Ian, just when i think i extracted myself from clogging this thread with Time-travelling Max Mercer, you've pulled me back in!<br /> -shakes fist melodramatically-<br /> <br /> I've been driven to create a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/465988-max-mercer-what-s-his-deal\">new discussion thread</a> for this purpose...</div> </div> </div> </div>You gave out before I did, Nihilist! *Nelson laugh* HAW HAW!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 04-02-2015, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T16:49:58-07:00","id":466665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=464600#post464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . Rape IS a special kind of evil . . . I can't even remember where it comes up in the 2008 source, to be completely honest. I'd ask One Vorlon to point it out, if i didn't already feel like i was so far off topic.. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>The rape/child vivisection comes up in the <b>Project Utopia</b> book. Its credited to one of the listed Proteus NPCs in the character glossary - and that one of the infants teleported away, right after telling him, &quot;too much light makes the baby go blind.&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T17:06:02-07:00","id":466677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=466665#post466665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rape/child vivisection comes up in the <b>Project Utopia</b> book. Its credited to one of the listed Proteus NPCs in the character glossary - and that one of the infants teleported away, right after telling him, &quot;too much light makes the baby go blind.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's. Friggin'. <i>Creepy</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T22:15:11-07:00","id":489064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463158#post463158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I've been putting off reading reading Nietzsche in favor of Machiavelli's The Prince, but now I have to read Nietzsche. I'm assuming the Ubermensch postulate is in <i>Men and Supermen</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm drawing from <b>Beyond Good and Evil</b>, actually. Interesting read, but he threw in a lot of criticism of ancient Greek playwrights. Technically, I understand why - he's trying to show the difference between an &quot;ar\u00eate&quot; (pursuit of excellence) based ethical code, and a good vs. evil moral one. But for the purposes of this discussion (on Mal), its kind of a pointless tangent.<br /> <br /> What is more relevant is that Nietzsche (and arguably Divis Mal) doesn't seem to think that morality can be &quot;fixed&quot;. Actually, he argues more for a social construct theory of &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; - the notion that winners write the history books, and public opinion ultimately decides what's &quot;right&quot; and 'wrong&quot;. Its a legitimate school of philosophical thought, but the idea that &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; aren't real tends to bug people. Which leaves both Nietzsche's ubermensch and Divis Mal open to accusations of being a sociopath. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what shocks me the most about all this is that Mercer, the leading founder of the Aeon Society, very likely foresaw all of this with his Timey Wimey Ball powers <i>and let it happen</i>. And the only reason a man like Mercer would have stood by and let all this happen is because any intervention on his part would have led to something <i>worse</i>.<br /> <br /> Just what the fuck did Mercer see to make him stand by and let World War II, the Holocaust, Proteus' atrocities, the Aberrant War <i>and </i>the Crash happen on his watch? What could be worse than all that? Did he somehow realize that if he tried to prevent all this, he'd somehow trigger the extinction of the human race?<br /> <br /> <i>What did Mercer see?</i> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Assuming Mercer's version of time travel is bound by the same rules as the nova form, then his ability to change history is very limited. According to the <b>Aberrant Player's Guide</b>, while a time traveler can rewrite history, history tends to fight back, trying to find &quot;alternate routes&quot; to the same key events. Plus, a time traveler's own presence tends to &quot;lock in&quot; the events, making them even tougher to change.<br /> <br /> So while Mercer could assassinate Hitler, for example, someone else from his inner circle would have simply seized the reigns of power, continuing World War II and the Holocaust. Same with the Aberrant War, or the rise of Proteus, or . . . .Something subtle or limited in scope won't cut it - he'd have to do something so drastic, history can't simply ignore it.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean he isn't trying, though. There are a number of odd coincidences throughout the setting that might be Mercer trying to &quot;fix&quot; things. Just how did Slider get the first hints of Proteus, for example? Or how did Sophia Rousseau know where to reach Corbin? Things like that might well be Mercer trying to limit the body count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T22:35:37-07:00","id":489069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=466677#post466677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's. Friggin'. <i>Creepy</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a talking self-aware infant with that level of nova powers is a tad disturbing. If I had to guess, the developers originally thought of Adam (the infant) as a stand-in for Divis Mal, someone who could lead the novas during the Aberrant War, should the players nuke Divis Mal. Incredibly powerful, with a very personal grudge against Aeon . . . . Sort of the way &quot;The Bug&quot; (NovaCom's hacker nova) could sub for Mungu Kuwasha or Synapse, in the battle that destroys the OpNet.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the existence of Adam raises the question of whether Divis Mal actually does all of the things (during the Aberrant War) that Aeon credits him with. If Divis Mal sees himself as the god of the Nova Age, Adam makes a very interesting messiah figure - and I could see Aeon fusing the two into the ultimate boogeyman (particularly to deflect questions about where Adam comes from). That whole line about &quot;Your legacy is our future&quot; never made much sense to me, coming from Divis Mal. It does makes sense, though, coming from a nova born purely as a lab animal, without any hint of compassion from the humans around him, who intended to vivisect him shortly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T13:26:54-07:00","id":615506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=489069#post489069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, a talking self-aware infant with that level of nova powers is a tad disturbing. If I had to guess, the developers originally thought of Adam (the infant) as a stand-in for Divis Mal, someone who could lead the novas during the Aberrant War, should the players nuke Divis Mal. Incredibly powerful, with a very personal grudge against Aeon . . . . Sort of the way &quot;The Bug&quot; (NovaCom's hacker nova) could sub for Mungu Kuwasha or Synapse, in the battle that destroys the OpNet.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the existence of Adam raises the question of whether Divis Mal actually does all of the things (during the Aberrant War) that Aeon credits him with. If Divis Mal sees himself as the god of the Nova Age, Adam makes a very interesting messiah figure - and I could see Aeon fusing the two into the ultimate boogeyman (particularly to deflect questions about where Adam comes from). That whole line about &quot;Your legacy is our future&quot; never made much sense to me, coming from Divis Mal. It does makes sense, though, coming from a nova born purely as a lab animal, without any hint of compassion from the humans around him, who intended to vivisect him shortly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where in the book is Adam mention?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6424,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","user":"Fuzzykuma","date":". 08-05-2015, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T18:01:24-07:00","id":623823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=103750#post103750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]He's using a level 6 power, Create Universe, which does exactly what it says on the tin. Using this power, the new universe one creates may have any physical laws or concepts of reality that one may conceive. A nova's new universe is in no way constrained by the physical laws of the nova's originating universe.[/LIST]As far as I know, there is no <i>official</i> mention that Michael/Divis Mal is associated with other White Wolf game lines and universes. What probably happened was that someone mentioned on a thread, saying &quot;Hey, wouldn't it be [awesome/hilarious/cool] if Divis Mal used Create Universe to make [Exalted's Creation/The Old World of Darkness/The New World of Darkness/a universe filled with chocolate/a place where he was the only one who had arms/etc.]?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairly sure that was me. Even made a thread on the old Vampire forum listing the similarities between Mal and the OWoDs creator. Sorry.<br /> <br /> As far as I remember discussions from the old forum, the Universe Creation power was written specificlly to take Mal out of the setting. At the end, he had become so powerful, the rest of the setting really didn't get a lot of relevance. The entrance to his unverse is in the heart of the Sun or something.<br /> <br /> In-character, Mal at last simply evolved past concern with humans and their worries. Much like we, evolved from single-celled organisms, no longer take much of a personal interest in the archebacterias concerns or priorities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=463158#post463158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And heaven help Aeon if the psiads ever find out about this. And despite Proteus destroying all their records and whitewashing the history of the Aberrant Era, that eventuality is <i>not </i>impossible. Correct me if I'm wrong, but The Colony was around during the Aberrant War, wasn't he? I remember reading somewhere that some people in Trinity were speculating that if The Colony had returned from deep space, then Divis Mal might still be around as well (even though Word of God says that Divis Mal is not coming back). Given that some novas are, compared to humans, very long-lived, then The Colony <i>can't</i> be the only nova alive in Trinity from the Aberrant era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Warfire was active from the first Aberrant Core rulebook to the last Trinity supplement. Hes the only named Aberrant I can remember that lasted from the war to still be active in Trinity. I suspect he may have had the greatest number of book apperances of any nova.<br /> <br /> The Colony was alive (if not conscious) quite early, well before the War, and probably participated. (Did anyone save the old &quot;What really happened&quot; from the old White Wolf site, with the war info? )<br /> As I remember, at the end of the previous game line one of the developers finally knuckled under to our incessant carping and gave us an/the origin for the Colony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 08-11-2015, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:36:45-07:00","id":626668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=623823#post623823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .The Colony was alive (if not conscious) quite early, well before the War, and probably participated. (Did anyone save the old &quot;What really happened&quot; from the old White Wolf site, with the war info? )<br /> As I remember, at the end of the previous game line one of the developers finally knuckled under to our incessant carping and gave us an/the origin for the Colony.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to a sidebar in the <b>Aberrant Player's Guide</b>, the Colony was around for the Aberrant War . . . but he was a nobody at the time. No known victories, defeats, or attrocities can be directly linked to him<br /> <br /> Which doesn't quite fit with the in-character blurbs from <b>Trinity</b>, where people seemed to immediately recognize the name and know who he (she?) was. Maybe the old forum posts can reconcile that . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T13:44:55-07:00","id":626940,"title":"","content":"From memory of posts made 10 years ago or so, the bit in the APG about vampiric eufibre was put in with the Colony in mind. The Colony started out as the vampiric eufibre of several powerful elites. While eufibre is normally a mindless organism, it does take on the wearers quantum signature and when enough mental mega-atttributes get imprinted...during some battle, enough of the eufibre got in physical contact to cross a threshold. And the Colony coalesced. A literal colony of vampiric eufibre.<br /> <br /> That is what I remember us being told. Whether it was made up on the spot or planned since the APG, I don't know. It has some interesting implications:<br /> <br /> The Colony is not human. The Colony<i> was never human</i>. Aberrants mostly started out as humans and have human memories and concerns. Even second-generation Aberrants have humanity in its very recent ancestry. The Colony is no closer to humanity than the bacteria that lives in your guts.<br /> <br /> The Colony is not an aberrant. The Colony <i>was</i> <i>never</i> a nova/aberrant.<br /> <br /> The Colony was begotten in pure violence, not sex of any kind.<br /> <br /> The Colony started out very, very powerful with the quantum signatures of several powerful elites.<br /> <br /> The Colony may be an exception to the rule about attributes and mega-attributes. It may have only mega-attributes, making for a cold and different mind indeed.<br /> <br /> And presumably, the Colony still needs to feed....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T13:57:03-07:00","id":626948,"title":"","content":"Ehhh. Cool concept, but for What is for all purposes the main Villain(Divis mal is gone, Doyen are distant threat at best, most others do not have gravitas) I find it kinda lacking. Gigantic flea of DOOOM is rather bland, especially after Abberant and Adventure with their very human evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:04:00-07:00","id":626959,"title":"","content":"More like some utterly alien thing sprung from human hubris.<br /> <br /> Oh, and before that fight that gave the eufibre critical mass...the colony was kindof around...but a quite literal nobody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:12:52-07:00","id":626962,"title":"","content":"Problem for me, Is that we already have alien things born out of human hubris, they are called Abberants. This take on colony is nothing new or interesting. It is just another empty Alien menace. It does not work for &quot;main&quot; villain of the piece. It is just variant of the rapey aliens, whose name I cannot remember right now. Only made by &quot;evil&quot; Abberants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:21:29-07:00","id":626969,"title":"","content":"I found it quite clever. Especially with the way the colony was around but with nothing linked to it -directly. Around, but no body. It takes a feature of the game and spins out a lot of interesting implications. Do the other aberrants know that the Colony isn't really one of them? No MR node, dressed in stolen qunatum finery? Does it still feed on them? Why does the Colony want to return? Can it reproduce?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:24:51-07:00","id":626970,"title":"","content":"Well, if we take into account, that to the best of my knowledge there are explicit children of the Colony conquering the chinese colony I think most of these answers is yes.<br /> <br /> edit: Also a lot of these questions relate to Abberants, who to the best of my knowledge of recent WoG are still not in the Aeon era as focus and core playable characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:28:48-07:00","id":626973,"title":"","content":"The Coalition is the name of the raped aliens.<br /> As for the Colony it has to have children as the Alpha Centarui colony was taken by the Colony who then left two of it's children in charge. I don't recall the whole vampire cloth becoming sentient but I do remember quite a bit of speculation that the creator of Eufiber was in actuality the Colony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:39:37-07:00","id":626984,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the name.<br /> This reminds me of campaign idea for &quot;Future Fallen&quot; setting I once had. Colony actually was master bioengineer, which specialized increating new lifeforms. All of these Abberant attackes on Earth were just seeding mision for its ultimate weapon. Non-quantum based bacteria, which could be long range strenghtened by quantum and they would then create might flowers all around the globe, which ar capable of Fusion reaction and are controlled by Colony. Story picks year, after Colony made landfall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T00:07:07-07:00","id":627318,"title":"","content":"Funny. I used vampiric eufiber as a recurrent 'venom' typed villain in my 2120s nova games, i played with the Colony being like this, but back then the books were still being published and i chose to leave the Colony to the sourcebooks, because i expected him to show up in one of the books eventually. Because i used this so long ago, i honestly have no idea if i came up with it myself or borrowed from a suggestion on a forum or just knew eufiber would be usable in a venom symbiote inspired story. I liked the idea that the handful of known 2120 'prime threats' weren't even always aberrants - some were AIs, cosmic strangers, bizarre telluric entities, avatars of greater mysteries, among others.<br /> The notion of a Comic-book end-of-the-world simply didn't gel in my head without some crazy infinite crisis scale going on - which was why Aeon were such a natural fit to form the Trinity about - as they have a long, storied past of highly dubious history. Even Max Mercer can't keep the full aberrant war straight in his head, like the ex-verminator sub-plot from Top Ten...<br /> I went to the trouble of finding a screenshot, but apparently i can't post attachments.<br /> -tiniest violin-<br /> Anyway, in those scales, leaving Mal to ferment in some alternate universe seemed wasteful and petty. Just to bring it back to the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T01:40:32-07:00","id":627370,"title":"","content":"Problem with Divis Mal as a player in Aeon is a desperate need to nerfbat him(good thing in my books, but you have to do that) and you will have to answer questions about Abberant war to explain his motivations somewhat and devs were understandably reluctant to do that. Him just abandoning earth and then coming back needs to be explained and him and his followers doing his own thing, and ignoring Earth does not make them players in Aeon, because per WoG it is Earth and Psion story, not Abberant one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T02:53:01-07:00","id":627409,"title":"","content":"The Aeon era story has little room for Divis Mal to drop by, i know it well.<br /> But in the peculiar instance of playing tainted novas in 2120, i had the room, if i needed it. Plus, the fear of Divis Mal's return can serve as a motivator for Psions - his art and background in the original books leave such an impression. When i first started playing, i had a couple of players who would have loved to quip one-liners and empty clips into that fiend, however wasteful that would have been as a use of the character. My brother still runs him as a villain, however conflicted and sympathetic, but since i never ran Aberrant or Adventure - i suppose i just never got a chance to really explore the character as deeply as i might have liked to - so sequestering him out of 2120 and 'replacing' him with the colony never appealed to me.<br /> It <i>could</i> have felt natural for a 'Battleground' type of strategy-driven campaign to roll over KLG, invade Chrome-Prime and finally chase down the Colony prior to the Coalition Ark arriving, <i>then</i> move onto the Prime Threats, eventually including Mal. Mal is a kind of end-boss, to those who like to play that way.<br /> -shrug-<br /> The thoughts of how others have used/interpreted the character during his active eras have made this thread a very interesting read and has just aggravated the soreness i felt losing the character from 2120. Sure he's powerful, but the source and this thread make a good case for him being mostly harmless outside of a few rare demonstrations and too alien by the 2120s to concern himself with human pettiness. Post-humanism taken through to godlike extremes has a place in Sci-Fi, what was once Mal may have another new identity by then - only peripherally occupied by his roots in humanity at best. But, the universe is a big place, no need to remove the character entirely - so i was happy his ultimate fate was never really confirmed anywhere important.<br /> P.S. What does WoG stand for? Word of God?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  post-script 08-15-2015, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T05:17:43-07:00","id":627486,"title":"","content":"Correct it stands for Word of God","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T08:28:27-07:00","id":627628,"title":"","content":"I'm actually a bit more sympathetic towards Divis Mal than I am to Mercer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T08:56:34-07:00","id":627642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=626668#post626668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to a sidebar in the <b>Aberrant Player's Guide</b>, the Colony was around for the Aberrant War . . . but he was a nobody at the time. No known victories, defeats, or attrocities can be directly linked to him<br /> <br /> Which doesn't quite fit with the in-character blurbs from <b>Trinity</b>, where people seemed to immediately recognize the name and know who he (she?) was. Maybe the old forum posts can reconcile that . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>*whistles innocently*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T12:04:47-07:00","id":627747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=627642#post627642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *whistles innocently*</div> </div> </div> </div>Now question stands. Is this whistle of infinite secret wisdom or do not notice the nonworking piece of lore one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T05:46:29-07:00","id":628476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=626940#post626940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From memory of posts made 10 years ago or so, the bit in the APG about vampiric eufibre was put in with the Colony in mind. The Colony started out as the vampiric eufibre of several powerful elites. While eufibre is normally a mindless organism, it does take on the wearers quantum signature and when enough mental mega-atttributes get imprinted...during some battle, enough of the eufibre got in physical contact to cross a threshold. And the Colony coalesced. A literal colony of vampiric eufibre.<br /> <br /> That is what I remember us being told. Whether it was made up on the spot or planned since the APG, I don't know. It has some interesting implications:<br /> <br /> The Colony is not human. The Colony<i> was never human</i>. Aberrants mostly started out as humans and have human memories and concerns. Even second-generation Aberrants have humanity in its very recent ancestry. The Colony is no closer to humanity than the bacteria that lives in your guts.<br /> <br /> The Colony is not an aberrant. The Colony <i>was</i> <i>never</i> a nova/aberrant.<br /> <br /> The Colony was begotten in pure violence, not sex of any kind.<br /> <br /> The Colony started out very, very powerful with the quantum signatures of several powerful elites.<br /> <br /> The Colony may be an exception to the rule about attributes and mega-attributes. It may have only mega-attributes, making for a cold and different mind indeed.<br /> <br /> And presumably, the Colony still needs to feed....</div> </div> </div> </div>From very long ago memory, I recall a popular theory being that the Colony was the Tainted evolution of Anibal Buendia, the originator of eufiber. As his mind twisted, he used his unique material to control Novas, and equipment - anything with eufiber in it. He implanted tendrils of the stuff into humans to boost and control them, much like the Colony would later do with sub-Aberrant mutants.<br /> <br /> I don't recall if this theory was ever refuted or endorsed by anyone with behind-the-scenes knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T07:29:26-07:00","id":628623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=627747#post627747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now question stands. Is this whistle of infinite secret wisdom or do not notice the nonworking piece of lore one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or is it the fact that the idea of the Colony being Buendia originated with Ian Watson. Chill would probably recall better than I since he ran the old TC site for quite some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T13:34:41-07:00","id":629042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=628623#post628623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or is it the fact that the idea of the Colony being Buendia originated with Ian Watson. Chill would probably recall better than I since he ran the old TC site for quite some time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That wasn't my idea, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T17:02:52-07:00","id":632832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=623823#post623823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Did anyone save the old &quot;What really happened&quot; from the old White Wolf site,</div> </div> </div> </div>By the power of the Wayback Machine: <b><a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020614160505/http://www.white-wolf.com/trinity.html\" target=\"_blank\">I HAVE THE POWER!</a> (</b>Although not ALL THE POWER.You need to go to the<b> &quot;Trinity Game Download&quot;</b> section and then click on the<b> &quot;Trinity: The story so far&quot;</b> link. That bt was always so well hidden that most people on the Trinity/Aberrant forums of the time didn't know about it.)<br /> <br /> Also <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020814153001fw_/http://www.white-wolf.com/trinityfiles/trinitychat1722001.html\" target=\"_blank\">a developer chat</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 08-19-2015, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T05:45:48-07:00","id":633352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=628623#post628623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or is it the fact that the idea of the Colony being Buendia originated with Ian Watson. Chill would probably recall better than I since he ran the old TC site for quite some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea, I didn't really pay much attention to Aberrant era stuff. That and I'm lazy / forgetful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T05:53:33-07:00","id":633358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=632832#post632832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the power of the Wayback Machine: <b><a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020614160505/http://www.white-wolf.com/trinity.html\" target=\"_blank\">I HAVE THE POWER!</a> (</b>Although not ALL THE POWER.You need to go to the<b> &quot;Trinity Game Download&quot;</b> section and then click on the<b> &quot;Trinity: The story so far&quot;</b> link. That bt was always so well hidden that most people on the Trinity/Aberrant forums of the time didn't know about it.)<br /> <br /> Also <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020814153001fw_/http://www.white-wolf.com/trinityfiles/trinitychat1722001.html\" target=\"_blank\">a developer chat</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that's a flashback - thanks for the link, that's a fun read <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, Colony = rival of Divis Mal, that's all the official stuff I can remember. I vaguely remember there being a fairly long debate on the EON forums about who the Colony was, but honestly I didn't take the time to read it (like, well, pretty much most of the Aberrant era related threads back on EON). I think this is an archive over on rpgpost.com of a lot of the old EON threads. Not sure how complete it is of if that thread is even in there: <a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/forum/126-trinity-continuum-rpg/?page=102\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.rpgpost.com/forum/126-tri...-rpg/?page=102</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T21:20:33-07:00","id":639835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=615506#post615506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where in the book is Adam mention?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adam is introduced on p. 138-139 of the <b>Project Utopia </b>book. He, his dead fraternal twin (Eva), and the Proteus experiment known as &quot;The Children&quot; are all part of the entry on Doctor Richard Toiho . . . with a bit more on The Children under the nova, &quot;Montressor&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T23:19:23-07:00","id":639890,"title":"","content":"I can't help but imagine that the big fight between Michael and Maxwell in WW2, that the both vanished during, happened in the early morning of July 16th, 1945 in the New Mexico desert outside Alamogordo - at a site called <i><b>Trinity</b></i>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Michael was trying to use the first man-made nuclear explosion to trigger world-wide eruption, and Maxwell as trying to stop him. This is the blast that threw Maxwell into the 22nd Century. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T03:23:23-07:00","id":641322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=639890#post639890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but imagine that the big fight between Michael and Maxwell in WW2, that the both vanished during, happened in the early morning of July 16th, 1945 in the New Mexico desert outside Alamogordo - at a site called <i><b>Trinity</b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's clever.<br /> It fits with Mal/Primoris' inferred goals, uses the era and adds a fun, pulpy element to the canon clash. I won't get into Maxwell's side here, but that's an interesting angle there too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T10:42:59-07:00","id":641807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal?p=639835#post639835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Adam is introduced on p. 138-139 of the <b>Project Utopia </b>book. He, his dead fraternal twin (Eva), and the Proteus experiment known as &quot;The Children&quot; are all part of the entry on Doctor Richard Toiho . . . with a bit more on The Children under the nova, &quot;Montressor&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I will hijack this. I kinda hope Adam and Co will get nuked out of the canon, together with idea of extreme increase of powers in second and third generation of Abberants. It just ties Nova too much and makes them too strong and thus too influential on the plot, even if they do not exist. I am not against the node brain idea, but imo that should make you more taint resistant, with price being slowed power increase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}